<h3 id=3D"1-ddl--data-definition-language" data-toc=3D"1. DDL =E2=80=94 Dat=
a Definition Language">1. DDL =E2=80=94 Data Definition Language</h3>
<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Define and modify the <em>structure</em> (sche=
ma) of the database =E2=80=94 tables, columns, indexes, constraints, etc.</=
p>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-important"><p class=3D"markdown=
-alert-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-report mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 =
16" version=3D"1.1" width=3D"16" height=3D"16" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=
=3D"M0 1.75C0 .784.784 0 1.75 0h12.5C15.216 0 16 .784 16 1.75v9.5A1.75 1.75=
 0 0 1 14.25 13H8.06l-2.573 2.573A1.458 1.458 0 0 1 3 14.543V13H1.75A1.75 1=
.75 0 0 1 0 11.25Zm1.75-.25a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v9.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h2a.=
75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.19l2.72-2.72a.749.749 0 0 1 .53-.22h6.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .=
25-.25v-9.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25-.25Zm7 2.25v2.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.5 0v-2.5a.75.75=
 0 0 1 1.5 0ZM9 9a1 1 0 1 1-2 0 1 1 0 0 1 2 0Z"></path></svg>Important</p><=
p><strong>Key idea:</strong> DDL doesn't touch the actual data rows. It dea=
ls with the <em>blueprint</em> =E2=80=94 what tables exist, what columns th=
ey have, what types those columns are, etc.</p>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"commands">Commands</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Command</th>
<th>What It Does</th>
<th>Syntax</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>CREATE</code></td>
<td>Creates a new database object (table, index, view, etc.)</td>
<td><code>CREATE TABLE table_name (col1 type, col2 type, ...);</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>ALTER</code></td>
<td>Modifies an existing object's structure</td>
<td><code>ALTER TABLE table_name ADD COLUMN col_name type;</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>DROP</code></td>
<td>Permanently deletes an object from the database</td>
<td><code>DROP TABLE table_name;</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>TRUNCATE</code></td>
<td>Removes <strong>all rows</strong> from a table (but keeps the table str=
ucture)</td>
<td><code>TRUNCATE TABLE table_name;</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>RENAME</code></td>
<td>Renames an existing object</td>
<td><code>RENAME TABLE old_name TO new_name;</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>COMMENT</code></td>
<td>Adds a descriptive comment to a table/column in the data dictionary</td=
>
<td><code>COMMENT ON TABLE table_name IS 'text';</code></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<h4 id=3D"example--creating-a-table">Example =E2=80=94 Creating a Table</h4=
>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keywor=
d">TABLE</span> employees (
    employee_id   <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-=
keyword">PRIMARY</span> KEY,
    first_name    <span class=3D"hljs-type">VARCHAR</span>(<span class=3D"h=
ljs-number">50</span>),
    last_name     <span class=3D"hljs-type">VARCHAR</span>(<span class=3D"h=
ljs-number">50</span>),
    department    <span class=3D"hljs-type">VARCHAR</span>(<span class=3D"h=
ljs-number">50</span>),
    hire_date     <span class=3D"hljs-type">DATE</span>
);</code></pre></div>
<p>This tells the database: <em>&quot;Create a container called <code>emplo=
yees</code> with these five columns and their data types.&quot;</em></p>
<h4 id=3D"truncate-vs-drop-vs-delete--a-common-confusion">TRUNCATE vs DROP =
vs DELETE =E2=80=94 A Common Confusion</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Aspect</th>
<th><code>TRUNCATE</code></th>
<th><code>DROP</code></th>
<th><code>DELETE</code> (DML)</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Removes rows?</td>
<td>=E2=9C=85 All rows</td>
<td>=E2=9C=85 All rows</td>
<td>=E2=9C=85 Selective or all</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Removes table structure?</td>
<td>=E2=9D=8C</td>
<td>=E2=9C=85</td>
<td>=E2=9D=8C</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Can use WHERE clause?</td>
<td>=E2=9D=8C</td>
<td>=E2=9D=8C</td>
<td>=E2=9C=85</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Can be rolled back?</td>
<td>=E2=9D=8C (auto-commits)</td>
<td>=E2=9D=8C (auto-commits)</td>
<td>=E2=9C=85 (within a transaction)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Speed</td>
<td>Very fast (deallocates pages)</td>
<td>Fast</td>
<td>Slower (row-by-row logging)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
