<h5 id=3D"production-strategy-3-bankers-rounding-for-financial-systems">Pro=
duction Strategy 3: Banker's Rounding (For Financial Systems)</h5>
<p>Standard rounding (<code>ROUND_HALF_UP</code>) always rounds <code>0.5</=
code> up: <code>2.5 becomes 3</code>, <code>3.5 becomes 4</code>. Over mill=
ions of transactions, this introduces a systematic upward bias.</p>
<p><strong>Banker's rounding</strong> (<code>ROUND_HALF_EVEN</code>) rounds=
 <code>0.5</code> to the nearest <strong>even</strong> number: <code>2.5 be=
comes 2</code>, <code>3.5 becomes 4</code>. Over many transactions, the rou=
nding errors cancel out statistically.</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">text</span></div><pre><code class=3D=
"hljs">Standard rounding:     2.5 -&gt; 3,  3.5 -&gt; 4,  4.5 -&gt; 5,  5.5=
 -&gt; 6   (always up)
Banker's rounding:     2.5 -&gt; 2,  3.5 -&gt; 4,  4.5 -&gt; 4,  5.5 -&gt; =
6   (alternates)</code></pre></div>
<p>MySQL's <code>ROUND()</code> function uses <strong>banker's rounding by =
default</strong> for exact-value types (<code>DECIMAL</code>):</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> ROUND(<span class=3D"hljs-=
number">2.5</span>);   <span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- 2  (rounds to even)<=
/span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> ROUND(<span class=3D"hljs-number=
">3.5</span>);   <span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- 4  (rounds to even)</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> ROUND(<span class=3D"hljs-number=
">4.5</span>);   <span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- 4  (rounds to even)</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> ROUND(<span class=3D"hljs-number=
">5.5</span>);   <span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- 6  (rounds to even)</span>=
</code></pre></div>
<p>In Java/Spring Boot, use <code>BigDecimal</code> with explicit rounding =
mode:</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">Java</span></div><pre><code class=3D=
"hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-type">BigDecimal</span> <span class=3D"hljs-vari=
able">price</span> <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"=
hljs-keyword">new</span> <span class=3D"hljs-title class_">BigDecimal</span=
>(<span class=3D"hljs-string">&quot;33.3333&quot;</span>);

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">// Banker&#x27;s rounding</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-type">BigDecimal</span> <span class=3D"hljs-variable">r=
ounded</span> <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> price.setScale(<span=
 class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>, RoundingMode.HALF_EVEN);  <span class=3D"h=
ljs-comment">// 33.33</span>

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">// Standard rounding</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-type">BigDecimal</span> <span class=3D"hljs-variable">r=
oundedUp</span> <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> price.setScale(<sp=
an class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>, RoundingMode.HALF_UP);  <span class=3D"h=
ljs-comment">// 33.33</span></code></pre></div>
