<h3 id=3D"the-migration-tracking-table" data-toc=3D"The Migration Tracking =
Table">The Migration Tracking Table</h3>
<p>Every ORM maintains a <strong>migrations table</strong> inside your data=
base to track which migrations have been applied:</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>ORM</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Tracking Table</th>
<th>What It Stores</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Prisma</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><code>_prisma_migrations</code></td>
<td>migration name, checksum (SHA256), timestamp</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Django</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><code>django_migrations</code></td>
<td>app name, migration name, timestamp</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Rails</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><code>schema_migrations</code></td>
<td>version (timestamp)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Sequelize</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><code>SequelizeMeta</code></td>
<td>migration filename</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>TypeORM</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><code>migrations</code></td>
<td>migration name, timestamp</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Flyway</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><code>flyway_schema_history</code></td>
<td>version, description, checksum, execution time</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p><strong>Why the checksum matters (Prisma):</strong> If you edit a migrat=
ion file that was already applied, the SHA256 hash won't match what's store=
d in <code>_prisma_migrations</code>. Prisma detects this <strong>drift</st=
rong> and refuses to proceed =E2=80=94 preventing silent corruption.</p>
<h3 id=3D"migration-commands-across-orms" data-toc=3D"Migration Commands Ac=
ross ORMs">Migration Commands Across ORMs</h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Action</th>
<th>Prisma</th>
<th>Django</th>
<th>Rails</th>
<th>Sequelize</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Create migration</strong></td>
<td><code>prisma migrate dev</code></td>
<td><code>python manage.py makemigrations</code></td>
<td><code>rails generate migration AddPhoneToUsers</code></td>
<td><code>npx sequelize migration:generate</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Apply migrations</strong></td>
<td><code>prisma migrate deploy</code></td>
<td><code>python manage.py migrate</code></td>
<td><code>rails db:migrate</code></td>
<td><code>npx sequelize db:migrate</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Check status</strong></td>
<td><code>prisma migrate status</code></td>
<td><code>python manage.py showmigrations</code></td>
<td><code>rails db:migrate:status</code></td>
<td><code>npx sequelize db:migrate:status</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Rollback</strong></td>
<td>=E2=9D=8C (manual)</td>
<td><code>python manage.py migrate app_name 0003</code></td>
<td><code>rails db:rollback</code></td>
<td><code>npx sequelize db:migrate:undo</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Reset DB</strong></td>
<td><code>prisma migrate reset</code></td>
<td><code>python manage.py flush</code></td>
<td><code>rails db:reset</code></td>
<td><code>npx sequelize db:migrate:undo:all</code></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<h3 id=3D"what-sql-does-a-migration-actually-generate" data-toc=3D"What SQL=
 Does a Migration Actually Generate?">What SQL Does a Migration Actually Ge=
nerate?</h3>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Adding a column</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ALTER</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">TABL=
E</span> users <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ADD</span> <span class=3D"hljs-=
keyword">COLUMN</span> phone <span class=3D"hljs-type">VARCHAR</span>(<span=
 class=3D"hljs-number">191</span>) <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">NULL</span>=
;

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Adding an index</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> INDEX idx_users_email <span clas=
s=3D"hljs-keyword">ON</span> users(email);

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Renaming a column</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ALTER</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">TABL=
E</span> users RENAME <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">COLUMN</span> name <span=
 class=3D"hljs-keyword">TO</span> full_name;

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Adding a foreign key</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ALTER</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">TABL=
E</span> orders <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ADD</span> <span class=3D"hljs=
-keyword">CONSTRAINT</span> fk_user=20
  <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FOREIGN</span> KEY (user_id) <span class=3D"=
hljs-keyword">REFERENCES</span> users(id) <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ON</=
span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">DELETE</span> CASCADE;

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Creating a new table</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">TAB=
LE</span> posts (
  id <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PRIM=
ARY</span> KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,
  title <span class=3D"hljs-type">VARCHAR</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-number=
">255</span>) <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">NOT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-k=
eyword">NULL</span>,
  user_id <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword"=
>NOT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">NULL</span>,
  <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FOREIGN</span> KEY (user_id) <span class=3D"=
hljs-keyword">REFERENCES</span> users(id)
);</code></pre></div>
