<p><strong>Common use cases for seeding:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Use Case</th>
<th>What Gets Seeded</th>
<th>Example</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Default/required data</strong></td>
<td>Data the app <em>needs</em> to function</td>
<td>Admin user, default roles (<code>admin</code>, <code>user</code>, <code=
>moderator</code>), countries list, categories</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Development data</strong></td>
<td>Fake data to test with locally</td>
<td>100 fake users, 500 sample products, dummy orders</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Testing data</strong></td>
<td>Predictable data for automated tests</td>
<td>Specific users with known IDs for test assertions</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Demo data</strong></td>
<td>Showcase data for demos/sales</td>
<td>Pre-built dashboards, sample reports</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<h3 id=3D"how-seeding-works--raw-sql" data-toc=3D"How Seeding Works =E2=80=
=94 Raw SQL">How Seeding Works =E2=80=94 Raw SQL</h3>
<p>At its simplest, seeding is just <code>INSERT</code> statements:</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Seed roles (required data =E2=80=94 a=
pp won&#x27;t work without these)</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INSERT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INT=
O</span> roles (name) <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">VALUES</span> (<span cla=
ss=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;admin&#x27;</span>), (<span class=3D"hljs-string">=
&#x27;editor&#x27;</span>), (<span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;viewer&#x27;=
</span>);

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Seed admin user</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INSERT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INT=
O</span> users (name, email, role_id)=20
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">VALUES</span> (<span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x=
27;Admin&#x27;</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;admin@example.com&=
#x27;</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">1</span>);

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Seed categories</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INSERT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INT=
O</span> categories (name, slug) <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">VALUES</span>=
=20
  (<span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;Electronics&#x27;</span>, <span class=
=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;electronics&#x27;</span>),
  (<span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;Clothing&#x27;</span>, <span class=3D"=
hljs-string">&#x27;clothing&#x27;</span>),
  (<span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;Books&#x27;</span>, <span class=3D"hlj=
s-string">&#x27;books&#x27;</span>);</code></pre></div>
<h3 id=3D"how-seeding-works-in-prisma" data-toc=3D"How Seeding Works in Pri=
sma">How Seeding Works in Prisma</h3>
<p>Prisma uses a dedicated <code>prisma/seed.ts</code> (or <code>.js</code>=
) file:</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">TypeScript</span></div><pre><code cl=
ass=3D"hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">// prisma/seed.ts</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">import</span> { <span class=3D"hljs-title clas=
s_">PrismaClient</span> } <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">from</span> <span cl=
ass=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;@prisma/client&#x27;</span>;

<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">const</span> prisma =3D <span class=3D"hljs-ke=
yword">new</span> <span class=3D"hljs-title class_">PrismaClient</span>();

<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">async</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">func=
tion</span> <span class=3D"hljs-title function_">main</span>(<span class=3D=
"hljs-params"></span>) {
  <span class=3D"hljs-comment">// Seed roles (upsert =3D create if not exis=
ts, update if exists)</span>
  <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">await</span> prisma.<span class=3D"hljs-prop=
erty">role</span>.<span class=3D"hljs-title function_">upsert</span>({
    <span class=3D"hljs-attr">where</span>: { <span class=3D"hljs-attr">nam=
e</span>: <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;admin&#x27;</span> },
    <span class=3D"hljs-attr">update</span>: {},
    <span class=3D"hljs-attr">create</span>: { <span class=3D"hljs-attr">na=
me</span>: <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;admin&#x27;</span> },
  });

  <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">await</span> prisma.<span class=3D"hljs-prop=
erty">role</span>.<span class=3D"hljs-title function_">upsert</span>({
    <span class=3D"hljs-attr">where</span>: { <span class=3D"hljs-attr">nam=
e</span>: <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;user&#x27;</span> },
    <span class=3D"hljs-attr">update</span>: {},
    <span class=3D"hljs-attr">create</span>: { <span class=3D"hljs-attr">na=
me</span>: <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;user&#x27;</span> },
  });

  <span class=3D"hljs-comment">// Seed admin user</span>
  <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">await</span> prisma.<span class=3D"hljs-prop=
erty">user</span>.<span class=3D"hljs-title function_">upsert</span>({
    <span class=3D"hljs-attr">where</span>: { <span class=3D"hljs-attr">ema=
il</span>: <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;admin@example.com&#x27;</span>=
 },
    <span class=3D"hljs-attr">update</span>: {},
    <span class=3D"hljs-attr">create</span>: {
      <span class=3D"hljs-attr">name</span>: <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#=
x27;Admin User&#x27;</span>,
      <span class=3D"hljs-attr">email</span>: <span class=3D"hljs-string">&=
#x27;admin@example.com&#x27;</span>,
      <span class=3D"hljs-attr">role</span>: { <span class=3D"hljs-attr">co=
nnect</span>: { <span class=3D"hljs-attr">name</span>: <span class=3D"hljs-=
string">&#x27;admin&#x27;</span> } },
    },
  });

  <span class=3D"hljs-variable language_">console</span>.<span class=3D"hlj=
s-title function_">log</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;=E2=9C=85 D=
atabase seeded!&#x27;</span>);
}

<span class=3D"hljs-title function_">main</span>()
  .<span class=3D"hljs-title function_">catch</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-fu=
nction">(<span class=3D"hljs-params">e</span>) =3D&gt;</span> { <span class=
=3D"hljs-variable language_">console</span>.<span class=3D"hljs-title funct=
ion_">error</span>(e); process.<span class=3D"hljs-title function_">exit</s=
pan>(<span class=3D"hljs-number">1</span>); })
  .<span class=3D"hljs-title function_">finally</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-=
function">() =3D&gt;</span> prisma.$disconnect());</code></pre></div>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">bash</span></div><pre><code class=3D=
"hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment"># Run the seed</span>
npx prisma db seed</code></pre></div>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note"><p class=3D"markdown-aler=
t-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-info mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" ver=
sion=3D"1.1" width=3D"16" height=3D"16" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M0 =
8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13=
ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 =
0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1=
 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z"></path></svg>Note</p><p><strong>Why <code>upsert</code=
>?</strong> It's <strong>idempotent</strong> =E2=80=94 you can run the seed=
 multiple times without creating duplicates. If the data already exists, it=
 skips or updates. This is crucial because seeds often run automatically af=
ter <code>prisma migrate reset</code>.</p>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"seed-commands-across-orms" data-toc=3D"Seed Commands Across ORMs"=
>Seed Commands Across ORMs</h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>ORM / Framework</th>
<th>Seed Command</th>
<th>Seed File Location</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Prisma</strong></td>
<td><code>npx prisma db seed</code></td>
<td><code>prisma/seed.ts</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Django</strong></td>
<td><code>python manage.py loaddata fixtures.json</code></td>
<td><code>app/fixtures/*.json</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Rails</strong></td>
<td><code>rails db:seed</code></td>
<td><code>db/seeds.rb</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Sequelize</strong></td>
<td><code>npx sequelize db:seed:all</code></td>
<td><code>seeders/*.js</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Laravel</strong></td>
<td><code>php artisan db:seed</code></td>
<td><code>database/seeders/*.php</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>TypeORM</strong></td>
<td>Custom script (no built-in)</td>
<td>Your own script</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<h3 id=3D"migration-vs-seeding--whats-the-difference" data-toc=3D"Migration=
 vs Seeding =E2=80=94 What's the Difference?">Migration vs Seeding =E2=80=
=94 What's the Difference?</h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th></th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Migration</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Seeding</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Changes</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Database <strong>structure</strong> (tables=
, columns, indexes)</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Database <strong>data</strong> (rows)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>SQL generated</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><code>CREATE TABLE</code>, <code>ALTER TABL=
E</code>, <code>DROP</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><code>INSERT INTO</code>, <code>UPDATE</cod=
e></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>When it runs</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Every environment (dev, staging, prod)</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Usually dev/test only</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Tracked?</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Versioned in migration table</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C Usually not tracked</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Idempotent?</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 (each migration runs once)</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Should be (use <code>upsert</code> / <code>=
INSERT IGNORE</code>)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
