p><strong>Key Takeaway:</strong> Migration creates the <strong>container</s=
trong> (tables/columns). Seeding fills the container with <strong>initial d=
ata</strong>. Migrations are mandatory everywhere; seeding is mostly for de=
v/test environments. Always make seeds idempotent (safe to run multiple tim=
es).</p>
