p><strong>The critical detail:</strong> MySQL applies <code>LIMIT</code>/<c=
ode>OFFSET</code> at the <strong>top</strong> of the execution plan, <em>af=
ter</em> rows have been materialized. It does <strong>not</strong> push &qu=
ot;skip 450,000&quot; down into the index scan. So every single skipped row=
 still pays for a full random-I/O row fetch =E2=80=94 and is then discarded=
.</p>
