<p>The mapping is one-to-one:</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>=F0=9F=93=9A Library</th>
<th>=F0=9F=97=84=EF=B8=8F MySQL</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>The card catalog drawer</td>
<td>The secondary index <code>(price, id)</code> =E2=80=94 small, sorted, d=
ensely packed</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>One index card</td>
<td>One index entry: <code>[sort column | primary key]</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>The shelf number written on the card</td>
<td>The <strong>primary key</strong> stored in every InnoDB secondary index=
 leaf</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>The actual book (heavy, 400 pages)</td>
<td>The <strong>full row</strong> in the clustered index</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Walking into the stacks to fetch a book</td>
<td>A random B+ Tree descent by PK =E2=80=94 <strong>the expensive part</st=
rong></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Flipping through cards in one drawer</td>
<td>Sequential index scan =E2=80=94 cheap</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Repeating the sort after fetching</td>
<td>The outer <code>ORDER BY</code> (books come back in shelf order, not au=
thor order)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
