<h3 id=3D"approach-3-cursor-based--keyset-pagination-the-right-way" data-to=
c=3D"Approach 3: Cursor-Based / Keyset Pagination (The =E2=80=A6">Approach =
3: Cursor-Based / Keyset Pagination (The Right Way)</h3>
<p>Instead of saying &quot;skip N rows&quot;, you say &quot;give me rows <s=
trong>after</strong> this specific value&quot;:</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Page 1 (first request, no cursor yet)=
</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-operator">*<=
/span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FROM</span> products <span class=3D"hlj=
s-keyword">ORDER</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">BY</span> id <span cla=
ss=3D"hljs-keyword">ASC</span> LIMIT <span class=3D"hljs-number">20</span>;
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Returns rows with id: 1, 2, 3, ... 20</span=
>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Last id =3D 20 =E2=86=92 this becomes the &=
quot;cursor&quot; for the next page</span>

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Page 2 (cursor =3D 20)</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-operator">*<=
/span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FROM</span> products <span class=3D"hlj=
s-keyword">WHERE</span> id <span class=3D"hljs-operator">&gt;</span> <span =
class=3D"hljs-number">20</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ORDER</span> <=
span class=3D"hljs-keyword">BY</span> id <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ASC</=
span> LIMIT <span class=3D"hljs-number">20</span>;
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Returns rows with id: 21, 22, ... 40</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- MySQL jumps DIRECTLY to id=3D20 using the i=
ndex =E2=86=92 O(log N)</span>

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Page 500 (cursor =3D 9980)</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-operator">*<=
/span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FROM</span> products <span class=3D"hlj=
s-keyword">WHERE</span> id <span class=3D"hljs-operator">&gt;</span> <span =
class=3D"hljs-number">9980</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ORDER</span>=
 <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">BY</span> id <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ASC=
</span> LIMIT <span class=3D"hljs-number">20</span>;
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Still just as fast! MySQL seeks to id=3D998=
0 in the B+ Tree index</span></code></pre></div>
<p><strong>Why it's fast:</strong> The <code>WHERE id &gt; cursor</code> us=
es the <strong>B+ Tree index</strong> to jump directly to the right positio=
n =E2=80=94 no scanning, no discarding. Performance is <strong>O(log N)</st=
rong> regardless of how deep you are.</p>
<h4 id=3D"handling-non-unique-sort-columns">Handling Non-Unique Sort Column=
s</h4>
<p>If you're sorting by a non-unique column (like <code>price</code>), you =
need a <strong>tiebreaker</strong> to avoid skipping/duplicating rows with =
the same value:</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- =E2=9D=8C WRONG =E2=80=94 rows with s=
ame price can be skipped or duplicated</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-operator">*<=
/span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FROM</span> products <span class=3D"hlj=
s-keyword">WHERE</span> price <span class=3D"hljs-operator">&gt;</span> <sp=
an class=3D"hljs-number">29.99</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ORDER</s=
pan> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">BY</span> price <span class=3D"hljs-keywo=
rd">ASC</span> LIMIT <span class=3D"hljs-number">20</span>;

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- =E2=9C=85 CORRECT =E2=80=94 use (price, id)=
 as a compound cursor</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-operator">*<=
/span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FROM</span> products=20
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> (price <span class=3D"hljs-operat=
or">&gt;</span> <span class=3D"hljs-number">29.99</span>) <span class=3D"hl=
js-keyword">OR</span> (price <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span=
 class=3D"hljs-number">29.99</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">AND</span>=
 id <span class=3D"hljs-operator">&gt;</span> <span class=3D"hljs-number">1=
042</span>)
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ORDER</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">BY</=
span> price <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ASC</span>, id <span class=3D"hljs=
-keyword">ASC</span>=20
LIMIT <span class=3D"hljs-number">20</span>;</code></pre></div>
<h4 id=3D"the-api-contract--what-you-send-the-frontend-what-the-frontend-se=
nds-back">The API Contract =E2=80=94 What You Send the Frontend, What the F=
rontend Sends Back</h4>
