<h3 id=3D"comparison" data-toc=3D"Comparison">Comparison</h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th></th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">OFFSET/LIMIT</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Deferred Join</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Cursor-Based (Keyset)</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Performance</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Degrades with depth =E2=80=94 O(OFFSET + LI=
MIT)</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Still O(OFFSET), but ~10=E2=80=9330=C3=97 s=
maller constant</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Constant =E2=80=94 O(log N) always</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>What it optimizes</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Nothing</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Avoids fetching rows it will discard</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Avoids <em>reading</em> skipped rows entire=
ly</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Data consistency</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C Duplicates/skips if data changes<=
/td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C Same problem =E2=80=94 it's still=
 OFFSET</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Stable for inserts/deletes (=E2=
=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F not if the sort <em>value</em> changes)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>&quot;Jump to page X&quot;</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Easy (<code>OFFSET =3D (page-1) *=
 size</code>)</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Yes =E2=80=94 keeps full OFFSET s=
emantics</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C Not natively supported</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Total count available</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Yes (with a <code>COUNT(*)</code>=
)</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Yes</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C Expensive / usually omitted</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Index requirement</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Helps, but OFFSET still scans</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>Must</strong> have an index coverin=
g the <code>ORDER BY</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>Must</strong> have an index on the =
cursor columns</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>UX style</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Numbered pages (1, 2, 3...)</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Numbered pages, but fast</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Infinite scroll / &quot;Load More&quot;</td=
>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Implementation</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Simple</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Simple (SQL-only change, API unchanged)</td=
>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Moderate (cursor encode/decode + API contra=
ct)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Best for</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Admin panels, small datasets, static report=
s</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Numbered-page UIs on large tables; wide row=
s</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">APIs, feeds, infinite scroll, large dataset=
s</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
