<h3 id=3D"three-schema-architecture-ansisparc" data-toc=3D"Three-Schema Arc=
hitecture (ANSI/SPARC)">Three-Schema Architecture (ANSI/SPARC)</h3>
<p>The three ideas above (the physical schema, the logical schema and sub-s=
chemas) are the three <strong>levels</strong> of the classic <strong>three-=
schema architecture</strong> (ANSI/SPARC, 1975). Its goal is to separate <e=
m>how users see data</em> from <em>how it's logically organised</em> from <=
em>how it's physically stored</em>, so that a change at one level doesn't r=
ipple into the others.</p>
