<h3 id=3D"what-operations-can-violate-referential-integrity" data-toc=3D"Wh=
at Operations Can Violate Referential Integrity?">What Operations Can Viola=
te Referential Integrity?</h3>
<h4 id=3D"on-the-child-table-employees">On the Child Table (employees)</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Operation</th>
<th>Violation?</th>
<th>Example</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>INSERT</code> with non-existent FK</td>
<td>=E2=9D=8C Rejected</td>
<td><code>INSERT INTO employees VALUES (105, 'Eve', 50)</code> =E2=80=94 de=
pt 50 doesn't exist</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>UPDATE</code> FK to non-existent value</td>
<td>=E2=9D=8C Rejected</td>
<td><code>UPDATE employees SET dept_id =3D 99 WHERE emp_id =3D 101</code> =
=E2=80=94 dept 99 doesn't exist</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>Child-side violations are <strong>always rejected</strong> =E2=80=94 no =
referential action can change that.</p>
<h4 id=3D"on-the-parent-table-departments">On the Parent Table (departments=
)</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Operation</th>
<th>Violation?</th>
<th>Example</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>DELETE</code> a row referenced by child</td>
<td>=E2=9D=8C Rejected (by default)</td>
<td><code>DELETE FROM departments WHERE dept_id =3D 10</code> =E2=80=94 Ali=
ce still references dept 10</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>UPDATE</code> PK that is referenced by child</td>
<td>=E2=9D=8C Rejected (by default)</td>
<td><code>UPDATE departments SET dept_id =3D 99 WHERE dept_id =3D 10</code>=
 =E2=80=94 Alice still points to 10</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>Parent-side operations raise the question: <em>&quot;What should happen =
to child rows when their referenced parent row is deleted or updated?&quot;=
</em> Foreign key <strong>referential actions</strong> answer this question=
.</p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"all-5-referential-actions" data-toc=3D"All 5 Referential Actions"=
>All 5 Referential Actions</h3>
<p>When defining a foreign key, you specify what should happen if the paren=
t row is deleted (<code>ON DELETE</code>) or its key is updated (<code>ON U=
PDATE</code>). The two clauses are independent, so you can mix them:</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FOREIGN</span> KEY (dept_id) <span class=
=3D"hljs-keyword">REFERENCES</span> departments(dept_id)
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ON</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">DEL=
ETE</span> CASCADE
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ON</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">UPD=
ATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SET</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyw=
ord">NULL</span></code></pre></div>
<h4 id=3D"1-cascade--propagate-the-change-to-children">1. <code>CASCADE</co=
de> =E2=80=94 Propagate the change to children</h4>
<p><strong><code>ON DELETE CASCADE</code></strong> =E2=80=94 When a parent =
row is deleted, <strong>automatically delete all child rows</strong> that r=
eference it.</p>
<p><strong>Before:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">emp_id</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">emp_name</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">dept_id</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">101</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Alice</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">10</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">102</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Bob</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">20</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">103</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Carol</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">30</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">DELETE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keywor=
d">FROM</span> departments <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> dept_i=
d <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-number">10</=
span>;
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- =E2=9C=85 All employees with dept_id =3D 10=
 are automatically deleted too</span></code></pre></div>
<p><strong>After (CASCADE):</strong> Alice is automatically deleted:</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">emp_id</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">emp_name</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">dept_id</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">102</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Bob</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">20</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">103</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Carol</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">30</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p><strong><code>ON UPDATE CASCADE</code></strong> =E2=80=94 When the paren=
t's primary key is updated, <strong>automatically update the foreign key</s=
trong> in all child rows.</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">UPDATE</span> departments <span class=3D=
"hljs-keyword">SET</span> dept_id <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> =
<span class=3D"hljs-number">99</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</s=
pan> dept_id <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-n=
umber">10</span>;
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- =E2=9C=85 All employees with dept_id =3D 10=
 (Alice) are automatically changed to dept_id =3D 99</span></code></pre></d=
iv>
<h4 id=3D"2-set-null--set-child-fk-to-null">2. <code>SET NULL</code> =E2=80=
=94 Set child FK to NULL</h4>
<p><strong><code>ON DELETE SET NULL</code></strong> =E2=80=94 When the pare=
nt is deleted, set the FK column in child rows to <code>NULL</code>.</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FOREIGN</span> KEY (dept_id) <span class=
=3D"hljs-keyword">REFERENCES</span> departments(dept_id) <span class=3D"hlj=
s-keyword">ON</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">DELETE</span> <span class=
=3D"hljs-keyword">SET</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">NULL</span>

<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">DELETE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FRO=
M</span> departments <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> dept_id <spa=
n class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-number">10</span>;
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Employees with dept_id =3D 10 now have dept=
_id =3D NULL (unassigned)</span></code></pre></div>
<p><strong>After (SET NULL):</strong> Alice's dept_id becomes NULL:</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">emp_id</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">emp_name</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">dept_id</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">101</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Alice</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">NULL</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">102</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Bob</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">20</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">103</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Carol</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">30</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p><strong><code>ON UPDATE SET NULL</code></strong> works the same way: cha=
nging the parent key sets the child FK to <code>NULL</code>.</p>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-warning"><p class=3D"markdown-a=
lert-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-alert mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16"=
 version=3D"1.1" width=3D"16" height=3D"16" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D=
"M6.457 1.047c.659-1.234 2.427-1.234 3.086 0l6.082 11.378A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 1=
4.082 15H1.918a1.75 1.75 0 0 1-1.543-2.575Zm1.763.707a.25.25 0 0 0-.44 0L1.=
698 13.132a.25.25 0 0 0 .22.368h12.164a.25.25 0 0 0 .22-.368Zm.53 3.996v2.5=
a.75.75 0 0 1-1.5 0v-2.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0ZM9 11a1 1 0 1 1-2 0 1 1 0 0 1 2=
 0Z"></path></svg>Warning</p><p>The FK column <strong>must allow NULLs</str=
ong> (<code>NOT NULL</code> will cause this to fail).</p>
</div>
<p><strong>Use case:</strong> The employee still exists but is temporarily =
unassigned to a department (just like Dave above).</p>
<h4 id=3D"3-restrict--block-the-operation">3. <code>RESTRICT</code> =E2=80=
=94 Block the operation</h4>
<p><strong><code>ON DELETE RESTRICT</code></strong> =E2=80=94 If any child =
rows reference the parent, <strong>refuse to delete</strong> the parent. Th=
rows an error immediately.</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FOREIGN</span> KEY (dept_id) <span class=
=3D"hljs-keyword">REFERENCES</span> departments(dept_id) <span class=3D"hlj=
s-keyword">ON</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">DELETE</span> RESTRICT

<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">DELETE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FRO=
M</span> departments <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> dept_id <spa=
n class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-number">10</span>;
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- =E2=9D=8C ERROR 1451: Cannot delete or upda=
te a parent row:</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- a foreign key constraint fails</span></code=
></pre></div>
<p>You must manually delete or reassign all employees first, then delete th=
e department. <code>ON UPDATE RESTRICT</code> likewise blocks changing a re=
ferenced parent key.</p>
<h4 id=3D"4-no-action--the-default-same-as-restrict-in-mysql">4. <code>NO A=
CTION</code> =E2=80=94 The default; same as RESTRICT in MySQL</h4>
<p>If you don't specify any action, the default is <strong><code>NO ACTION<=
/code></strong>. In MySQL, <code>NO ACTION</code> behaves <strong>identical=
ly</strong> to <code>RESTRICT</code>. Both block the operation if child row=
s exist =E2=80=94 so in practice, <strong>blocking is the default behavior<=
/strong>.</p>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note"><p class=3D"markdown-aler=
t-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-info mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" ver=
sion=3D"1.1" width=3D"16" height=3D"16" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M0 =
8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13=
ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 =
0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1=
 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z"></path></svg>Note</p><p>In some other databases (Postg=
reSQL), <code>RESTRICT</code> checks immediately, while <code>NO ACTION</co=
de> checks at the <strong>end of the statement</strong> =E2=80=94 and, if t=
he constraint is declared <code>DEFERRABLE</code>, can be deferred to the <=
strong>end of the transaction</strong>. MySQL doesn't support deferred chec=
ks, so they're the same.</p>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"5-set-default--set-fk-to-its-default-value">5. <code>SET DEFAULT<=
/code> =E2=80=94 Set FK to its default value</h4>
<p><strong><code>ON DELETE SET DEFAULT</code></strong> =E2=80=94 Sets the c=
hild FK to its column default value when the parent is deleted (<code>ON UP=
DATE SET DEFAULT</code> does the same on a key change).</p>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-warning"><p class=3D"markdown-a=
lert-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-alert mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16"=
 version=3D"1.1" width=3D"16" height=3D"16" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D=
"M6.457 1.047c.659-1.234 2.427-1.234 3.086 0l6.082 11.378A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 1=
4.082 15H1.918a1.75 1.75 0 0 1-1.543-2.575Zm1.763.707a.25.25 0 0 0-.44 0L1.=
698 13.132a.25.25 0 0 0 .22.368h12.164a.25.25 0 0 0 .22-.368Zm.53 3.996v2.5=
a.75.75 0 0 1-1.5 0v-2.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0ZM9 11a1 1 0 1 1-2 0 1 1 0 0 1 2=
 0Z"></path></svg>Warning</p><p><strong>InnoDB does NOT support <code>SET D=
EFAULT</code></strong>. MySQL parses it but will throw an error if you try =
to use it with InnoDB. This exists mainly in the SQL standard and in other =
databases.</p>
</div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"side-by-side-comparison" data-toc=3D"Side-by-Side Comparison">Sid=
e-by-Side Comparison</h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Action</th>
<th>On Parent DELETE</th>
<th>On Parent UPDATE</th>
<th>When to Use</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong><code>CASCADE</code></strong></td>
<td>Delete all children</td>
<td>Update FK in all children</td>
<td>Child has no meaning without parent (order items =E2=86=92 order)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong><code>SET NULL</code></strong></td>
<td>Set FK to <code>NULL</code></td>
<td>Set FK to <code>NULL</code></td>
<td>Child can exist independently (employee =E2=86=92 department)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong><code>RESTRICT</code></strong></td>
<td>=E2=9D=8C Block the delete</td>
<td>=E2=9D=8C Block the update</td>
<td>Must handle children explicitly before deleting parent</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong><code>NO ACTION</code></strong> (default)</td>
<td>=E2=9D=8C Block =E2=80=94 same as RESTRICT in MySQL</td>
<td>=E2=9D=8C Block =E2=80=94 same as RESTRICT in MySQL</td>
<td>Same as above</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong><code>SET DEFAULT</code></strong></td>
<td>Set FK to its default value</td>
<td>Set FK to its default value</td>
<td>=E2=9D=8C Not supported in InnoDB</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"real-world-examples" data-toc=3D"Real-World Examples">Real-World =
Examples</h3>
<h4 id=3D"e-commerce--cascade-makes-sense">E-Commerce =E2=80=94 <code>CASCA=
DE</code> makes sense</h4>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keywor=
d">TABLE</span> orders (
    id <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PR=
IMARY</span> KEY,
    customer_id <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span>,
    total <span class=3D"hljs-type">DECIMAL</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-numb=
er">10</span>,<span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>)
);

<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">TAB=
LE</span> order_items (
    id <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PR=
IMARY</span> KEY,
    order_id <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span>,
    product_name <span class=3D"hljs-type">VARCHAR</span>(<span class=3D"hl=
js-number">100</span>),
    quantity <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span>,
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FOREIGN</span> KEY (order_id) <span class=
=3D"hljs-keyword">REFERENCES</span> orders(id)
        <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ON</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword"=
>DELETE</span> CASCADE    <span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Delete order =E2=
=86=92 delete all its items</span>
);</code></pre></div>
<p><strong>Why CASCADE?</strong> An order item has <strong>no meaning</stro=
ng> without its order. If the order is deleted, keeping orphaned items make=
s no sense.</p>
<h4 id=3D"hr-system--set-null-makes-sense">HR System =E2=80=94 <code>SET NU=
LL</code> makes sense</h4>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keywor=
d">TABLE</span> managers (
    id <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PR=
IMARY</span> KEY,
    name <span class=3D"hljs-type">VARCHAR</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-numbe=
r">100</span>)
);

<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">TAB=
LE</span> employees (
    id <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PR=
IMARY</span> KEY,
    name <span class=3D"hljs-type">VARCHAR</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-numbe=
r">100</span>),
    manager_id <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-key=
word">NULL</span>,
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FOREIGN</span> KEY (manager_id) <span clas=
s=3D"hljs-keyword">REFERENCES</span> managers(id)
        <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ON</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword"=
>DELETE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SET</span> <span class=3D"hljs-=
keyword">NULL</span>   <span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Manager leaves =E2=
=86=92 employees become unassigned</span>
);</code></pre></div>
<p><strong>Why SET NULL?</strong> Employees don't get fired when their mana=
ger leaves. They just temporarily have no manager.</p>
<h4 id=3D"banking--restrict-makes-sense">Banking =E2=80=94 <code>RESTRICT</=
code> makes sense</h4>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keywor=
d">TABLE</span> accounts (
    id <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PR=
IMARY</span> KEY,
    balance <span class=3D"hljs-type">DECIMAL</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-nu=
mber">15</span>,<span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>)
);

<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">TAB=
LE</span> transactions (
    id <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PR=
IMARY</span> KEY,
    account_id <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span>,
    amount <span class=3D"hljs-type">DECIMAL</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-num=
ber">10</span>,<span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>),
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FOREIGN</span> KEY (account_id) <span clas=
s=3D"hljs-keyword">REFERENCES</span> accounts(id)
        <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ON</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword"=
>DELETE</span> RESTRICT   <span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Cannot delete acc=
ount if it has transactions</span>
);</code></pre></div>
<p><strong>Why RESTRICT?</strong> Financial records must never be silently =
deleted. You must explicitly handle or archive transactions before closing =
an account.</p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"what-happens-if-you-dont-use-fk-constraints" data-toc=3D"What Hap=
pens If You Don't Use FK Constraints?">What Happens If You Don't Use FK Con=
straints?</h3>
<p>If you define a foreign key but don't specify <code>ON DELETE</code> / <=
code>ON UPDATE</code>, MySQL defaults to <strong><code>NO ACTION</code></st=
rong> (which behaves as <code>RESTRICT</code>). But if you skip defining fo=
reign keys entirely, things get worse:</p>
<h4 id=3D"problem-1-orphaned-rows-silent-data-corruption">Problem 1: Orphan=
ed rows (silent data corruption)</h4>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- No FK defined =E2=80=94 just a plain =
column</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">TAB=
LE</span> order_items (
    id <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PR=
IMARY</span> KEY,
    order_id <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span>,             <span class=
=3D"hljs-comment">-- no foreign key constraint!</span>
    product_name <span class=3D"hljs-type">VARCHAR</span>(<span class=3D"hl=
js-number">100</span>)
);

<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">DELETE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FRO=
M</span> orders <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> id <span class=3D=
"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-number">42</span>;
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- =E2=9C=85 Succeeds... but order_items with =
order_id =3D 42 are now ORPHANS</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- They reference a non-existent order</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- JOINs return nothing, reports are wrong, da=
ta is silently broken</span></code></pre></div>
<h4 id=3D"problem-2-manual-cleanup-everywhere">Problem 2: Manual cleanup ev=
erywhere</h4>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Without CASCADE, deleting an order re=
quires multiple steps:</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">DELETE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FRO=
M</span> order_items <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> order_id <sp=
an class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-number">42</span>=
;    <span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Step 1</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">DELETE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FRO=
M</span> order_shipping <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> order_id =
<span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-number">42</sp=
an>; <span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Step 2</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">DELETE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FRO=
M</span> order_payments <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> order_id =
<span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-number">42</sp=
an>; <span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Step 3</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">DELETE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FRO=
M</span> orders <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> id <span class=3D=
"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-number">42</span>;          =
     <span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Step 4: FINALLY the parent</span>

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- With CASCADE, it&#x27;s just:</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">DELETE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FRO=
M</span> orders <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> id <span class=3D=
"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-number">42</span>;          =
     <span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Done. Everything cleaned up.</span></c=
ode></pre></div>
<h4 id=3D"problem-3-application-level-enforcement-is-fragile">Problem 3: Ap=
plication-level enforcement is fragile</h4>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">Java</span></div><pre><code class=3D=
"hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">// =E2=9D=8C Fragile =E2=80=94 what if =
someone runs raw SQL or a migration script?</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-meta">@Transactional</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">public</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">voi=
d</span> <span class=3D"hljs-title function_">deleteOrder</span><span class=
=3D"hljs-params">(Long orderId)</span> {
    orderItemRepository.deleteByOrderId(orderId);     <span class=3D"hljs-c=
omment">// hope you didn&#x27;t forget</span>
    orderShippingRepository.deleteByOrderId(orderId);  <span class=3D"hljs-=
comment">// and this</span>
    orderRepository.deleteById(orderId);
}</code></pre></div>
<p>Anyone who bypasses your application (raw SQL, a DBA, another microservi=
ce) can break the data. <strong>Database-level FK constraints are the last =
line of defense.</strong></p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"do-fk-actions-fix-anomalies" data-toc=3D"Do FK Actions Fix Anomal=
ies?">Do FK Actions Fix Anomalies?</h3>
<p><strong>No.</strong> They solve a <strong>different problem</strong> (se=
e <a href=3D"#database-anomalies">Database Anomalies</a>):</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Problem</th>
<th>Cause</th>
<th>Solution</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Anomalies</strong> (insertion, deletion, update)</td>
<td>Everything crammed into one table with redundant data</td>
<td><strong>Normalization</strong> =E2=80=94 split into multiple tables</td=
>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Orphaned/inconsistent references</strong></td>
<td>Multiple tables exist but relationships aren't enforced</td>
<td><strong>FK constraints</strong> with <code>CASCADE</code> / <code>SET N=
ULL</code> / <code>RESTRICT</code></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p><strong>Normalization</strong> creates the proper multi-table structure =
(fixing anomalies). <strong>FK actions</strong> then protect that structure=
 from breaking. They're <strong>complementary</strong> =E2=80=94 normalizat=
ion solves the design problem, FK constraints solve the integrity problem.<=
/p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"summary--quick-decision-guide" data-toc=3D"Summary &amp; Quick De=
cision Guide">Summary &amp; Quick Decision Guide</h3>
<h4 id=3D"summary">Summary</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Rule</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Referential Integrity</strong></td>
<td>FK must match an existing PK in the parent table, or be NULL</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Purpose</strong></td>
<td>Prevent orphan records and ensure data consistency across related table=
s</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Enforced by</strong></td>
<td><code>FOREIGN KEY</code> constraint in table definition</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Violation handling</strong></td>
<td><code>CASCADE</code>, <code>SET NULL</code>, <code>SET DEFAULT</code>, =
<code>RESTRICT</code>, or <code>NO ACTION</code> (default)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<h4 id=3D"quick-decision-guide-1">Quick Decision Guide</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Relationship</th>
<th>Recommended Action</th>
<th>Reason</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Order =E2=86=92 Order Items</td>
<td><code>ON DELETE CASCADE</code></td>
<td>Items are meaningless without the order</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>User =E2=86=92 Posts</td>
<td><code>ON DELETE CASCADE</code> or <code>SET NULL</code></td>
<td>CASCADE to remove; SET NULL to keep as &quot;deleted user&quot;</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Employee =E2=86=92 Department</td>
<td><code>ON DELETE SET NULL</code></td>
<td>Employee survives without a department</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Account =E2=86=92 Transactions</td>
<td><code>ON DELETE RESTRICT</code></td>
<td>Never silently delete financial records</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Category =E2=86=92 Products</td>
<td><code>ON DELETE RESTRICT</code></td>
<td>Force admin to reassign products first</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Comment =E2=86=92 Replies</td>
<td><code>ON DELETE CASCADE</code></td>
<td>Replies to a deleted comment should be removed</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Parent PK changes</td>
<td><code>ON UPDATE CASCADE</code></td>
<td>Rare =E2=80=94 avoid changing PKs. Use surrogate keys (auto-increment)<=
/td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
