</section><section class=3D"sec"><h2 id=3D"three-relationship-types-in-er-m=
odeling" data-toc=3D"10. Three Relationship Types in ER Modeling"><span cla=
ss=3D"sec-n">10.</span> Three Relationship Types in ER Modeling</h2>
<p>Entity-Relationship (ER) diagrams model how entities relate to each othe=
r. In practice, almost every design choice =E2=80=94 keys, foreign keys, ju=
nction tables =E2=80=94 follows from the <strong>type of relationship</stro=
ng> and whether participation is optional or mandatory.</p>
<p>=F0=9F=94=97 <a href=3D"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/dbms/introduction-=
of-er-model/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener">GeeksforGeeks =E2=80=94 In=
troduction of ER Model</a></p>
<hr>
