<h5 id=3D"many-to-one-n1--just-the-inverse-view">Many-to-One (N:1) =E2=80=
=94 Just the Inverse View</h5>
<p>N:1 is the same relationship as 1:N, just viewed from the other directio=
n:</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Viewpoint</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>1:N (Department =E2=86=92 Employees)</td>
<td>One department has many employees</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>N:1 (Employees =E2=86=92 Department)</td>
<td>Many employees map to one department</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>Same table design, same FK =E2=80=94 just a different perspective.</p>
<hr>
<h4 id=3D"3-many-to-many-mn">3. Many-to-Many (M:N)</h4>
