 must belong to a Department (mandatory/total, min 1 max 1); Department may=
 have zero employees (optional/partial, min 0 max N); UML  1..1  to  0..*" =
loading=3D"lazy"></figure>
<p><strong>Impact on schema:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Mandatory participation</strong> =E2=86=92 use <code>NOT NULL</=
code> on the FK</li>
<li><strong>Optional participation</strong> =E2=86=92 allow <code>NULL</cod=
e> on the FK</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"notation-cheat-sheet" data-toc=3D"Notation Cheat Sheet">Notation =
Cheat Sheet</h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Concept</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Chen Notation</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Crow's Foot</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">UML</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>One</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><code>1</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Single bar <code>=E2=94=82</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><code>1</code> or <code>0..1</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Many</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><code>N</code> or <code>M</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Crow's foot <code>&gt;=E2=94=80</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><code>*</code> or <code>0..*</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Mandatory</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Annotation</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Single bar <code>=E2=94=82</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Lower bound =E2=89=A5 1 (e.g., <code>1..1</=
code>)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Optional</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Annotation</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Open circle <code>=E2=97=8B</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Lower bound =3D 0 (e.g., <code>0..1</code>)=
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note"><p class=3D"markdown-aler=
t-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-info mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" ver=
sion=3D"1.1" width=3D"16" height=3D"16" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M0 =
8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13=
ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 =
0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1=
 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z"></path></svg>Note</p><p><strong>FAQ:</strong> <code>1.=
.*</code> (UML) and <code>1:N</code> (ER) both mean one-to-many. UML makes =
optionality explicit via the lower bound (e.g., <code>0..*</code> =3D optio=
nal-many vs <code>1..*</code> =3D mandatory-many).</p>
</div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"relational-implementation-patterns--summary" data-toc=3D"Relation=
al Implementation Patterns =E2=80=94 Summary">Relational Implementation Pat=
terns =E2=80=94 Summary</h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Relationship</th>
<th>Where to Put FK</th>
<th>Key Constraints</th>
<th>Notes</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>1:N</strong></td>
<td>FK on the N-side referencing the 1-side</td>
<td><code>NOT NULL</code> if mandatory; index the FK</td>
<td>Most common pattern</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>1:1</strong></td>
<td>FK on either side with <code>UNIQUE</code> constraint</td>
<td>Or share the PK across both tables</td>
<td>Choose based on ownership/optionality</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>M:N</strong></td>
<td>Create a junction table with two FKs</td>
<td>Composite PK <code>(A_id, B_id)</code> or surrogate key + UNIQUE</td>
<td>Store relationship attributes here</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"everyday-examples" data-toc=3D"Everyday Examples">Everyday Exampl=
es</h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Type</th>
<th>Example</th>
<th>Implementation</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>1:1</strong></td>
<td>A vehicle has at most one title; a title applies to at most one vehicle=
</td>
<td>FK with UNIQUE or shared PK</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>1:N</strong></td>
<td>A customer places many orders; each order belongs to one customer</td>
<td>FK (<code>customer_id</code>) in <code>orders</code> table</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>M:N</strong></td>
<td>A student enrolls in many classes; a class has many students</td>
<td>Junction table <code>enrollment(student_id, class_id)</code></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note"><p class=3D"markdown-aler=
t-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-info mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" ver=
sion=3D"1.1" width=3D"16" height=3D"16" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M0 =
8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13=
ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 =
0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1=
 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z"></path></svg>Note</p><p><strong>In real systems</stron=
g>, 1:N and M:N dominate. True 1:1 is rarer and usually modeled for lifecyc=
le, security, or sparsity reasons.</p>
</div>
