<h3 id=3D"1-super-key" data-toc=3D"1. Super Key">1. Super Key</h3>
<p>A <strong>super key</strong> is any set of one or more columns that can =
<strong>uniquely identify every row</strong> in a table. It may contain ext=
ra (redundant) columns.</p>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note"><p class=3D"markdown-aler=
t-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-info mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" ver=
sion=3D"1.1" width=3D"16" height=3D"16" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M0 =
8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13=
ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 =
0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1=
 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z"></path></svg>Note</p><p><strong>Think of it as:</stron=
g> &quot;Any combination that is enough to uniquely find a student =E2=80=
=94 even if you're using more columns than necessary.&quot;</p>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"super-keys-for-students">Super Keys for <code>students</code>:</h=
4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Super Key</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Unique?</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Minimal?</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>{roll_no}</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 (also a candidate key)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>{email}</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 (also a candidate key)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>{phone}</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 (also a candidate key)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>{roll_no, name}</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C (<code>name</code> is redundant =
=E2=80=94 <code>roll_no</code> alone is enough)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>{roll_no, email}</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85</td>
