<h4 id=3D"foreign-key-properties">Foreign Key Properties:</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Property</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Can have <strong>duplicate values</strong></td>
<td>Multiple students can be in the same department</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Can be <strong>NULL</strong></td>
<td>A student might not be assigned to any department yet</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Must match a <strong>PK value</strong> in the parent table (or be NULL)=
</td>
<td>Referential integrity</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>A table can have <strong>multiple FKs</strong></td>
<td>e.g., <code>students</code> could also FK to an <code>advisor</code> ta=
ble</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keywor=
d">TABLE</span> students (
    roll_no  <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keywo=
rd">PRIMARY</span> KEY,
    name     <span class=3D"hljs-type">VARCHAR</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-n=
umber">50</span>),
    dept     <span class=3D"hljs-type">VARCHAR</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-n=
umber">10</span>),
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FOREIGN</span> KEY (dept) <span class=3D"h=
ljs-keyword">REFERENCES</span> departments(dept_id)
);</code></pre></div>
<p>What the database does when a referenced parent row is deleted or update=
d (<code>CASCADE</code>, <code>SET NULL</code>, <code>RESTRICT</code>, =E2=
=80=A6) is covered in <a href=3D"#referential-integrity--foreign-key-action=
s-on-delete--on-update">Referential Integrity &amp; Foreign Key Actions</a>=
.</p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"6-secondary-key-search-key" data-toc=3D"6. Secondary Key (Search =
Key)">6. Secondary Key (Search Key)</h3>
<p>A <strong>secondary key</strong> is any column used frequently for <stro=
ng>searching or looking up</strong> data, but which is NOT the primary key.=
 It doesn't need to be unique.</p>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note"><p class=3D"markdown-aler=
t-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-info mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" ver=
sion=3D"1.1" width=3D"16" height=3D"16" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M0 =
8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13=
ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 =
0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1=
 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z"></path></svg>Note</p><p><strong>Think of it as:</stron=
g> &quot;Not the official ID, but a column you search by often =E2=80=94 so=
 you index it for speed.&quot;</p>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"secondary-keys-for-students">Secondary Keys for <code>students</c=
ode>:</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Column</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">PK?</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Often searched?</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Secondary Key?</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><code>roll_no</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 PK</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=80=94</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">No (it's the PK)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><code>name</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 &quot;Find students named Alice&q=
uot;</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 <strong>Secondary Key</strong></t=
d>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><code>dept</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 &quot;Find all CSE students&quot;=
</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 <strong>Secondary Key</strong></t=
d>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><code>email</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Sometimes</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Possibly</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p><strong>In practice</strong>, you create an <strong>index</strong> on se=
condary keys to speed up queries:</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- These columns are searched often, so =
index them</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> INDEX idx_student_name <span cla=
ss=3D"hljs-keyword">ON</span> students(name);
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> INDEX idx_student_dept <span cla=
ss=3D"hljs-keyword">ON</span> students(dept);</code></pre></div>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-important"><p class=3D"markdown=
-alert-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-report mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 =
16" version=3D"1.1" width=3D"16" height=3D"16" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=
=3D"M0 1.75C0 .784.784 0 1.75 0h12.5C15.216 0 16 .784 16 1.75v9.5A1.75 1.75=
