</section><section class=3D"sec"><h2 id=3D"sql-views" data-toc=3D"13. SQL V=
iews"><span class=3D"sec-n">13.</span> SQL Views</h2>
<p>A <strong>View</strong> is a <strong>virtual table</strong> created from=
 a <code>SELECT</code> query. It does NOT store data physically =E2=80=94 i=
t's just a saved query that behaves like a table. Every time you query a vi=
ew, the underlying <code>SELECT</code> runs and fetches fresh data.</p>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note"><p class=3D"markdown-aler=
t-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-info mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" ver=
sion=3D"1.1" width=3D"16" height=3D"16" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M0 =
8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13=
ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 =
0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1=
 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z"></path></svg>Note</p><p><strong>Think of it this way:<=
/strong> A view is like a <strong>saved bookmark</strong> for a complex que=
ry. Instead of writing the same long query every time, you give it a name a=
nd reuse it like a table.</p>
</div>
