</section><section class=3D"sec"><h2 id=3D"sql-triggers" data-toc=3D"14. SQ=
L Triggers"><span class=3D"sec-n">14.</span> SQL Triggers</h2>
<p>A <strong>trigger</strong> is a special stored procedure that <strong>ru=
ns automatically</strong> when an <code>INSERT</code>, <code>UPDATE</code>,=
 or <code>DELETE</code> (or DDL) operation occurs on a table. You don't cal=
l a trigger =E2=80=94 it fires on its own when the specified event happens.=
</p>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note"><p class=3D"markdown-aler=
t-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-info mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" ver=
sion=3D"1.1" width=3D"16" height=3D"16" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M0 =
8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13=
ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 =
0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1=
 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z"></path></svg>Note</p><p><strong>Think of it this way:<=
/strong> A trigger is like a <strong>motion sensor light</strong> =E2=80=94=
 you don't press a switch; it turns on automatically when it detects moveme=
nt (an event).</p>
</div>
