<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- List all procedures (MySQL)</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SHOW</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PROCE=
DURE</span> STATUS <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> Db <span class=
=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;your_databa=
se&#x27;</span>;

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Show procedure code</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SHOW</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREAT=
E</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PROCEDURE</span> procedure_name;

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Drop a procedure</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">DROP</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PROCE=
DURE</span> IF <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">EXISTS</span> procedure_name;</=
code></pre></div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"stored-procedure-vs-function-vs-trigger" data-toc=3D"Stored Proce=
dure vs Function vs Trigger">Stored Procedure vs Function vs Trigger</h3>
<p>Now that both triggers and stored procedures are introduced, here is how=
 they compare with each other (and with functions):</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Aspect</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Stored Procedure</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Function</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Trigger</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>How it runs</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Called <strong>explicitly</strong> (<code>C=
ALL</code>)</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Called in expressions (<code>SELECT fn()</c=
ode>)</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Fires <strong>automatically</strong> on eve=
nts (<code>INSERT</code>/<code>UPDATE</code>/<code>DELETE</code>)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Tied to a table event?</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C No =E2=80=94 standalone, invoked =
whenever you want</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C No</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Yes =E2=80=94 always bound to a t=
able + event</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Accepts parameters?</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Yes (<code>IN</code>, <code>OUT</=
code>, <code>INOUT</code>)</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Yes (inputs)</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C No (only gets <code>OLD</code>/<c=
ode>NEW</code> row values)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Returns</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Zero or more result sets, <code>OUT</code> =
params</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Exactly one value</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Nothing (side effects only)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Can modify data?</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Yes (INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE)</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C Usually no (read-only)</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Yes</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Can use transactions?</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Yes (COMMIT/ROLLBACK)</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C No</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F Limited</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Can be called directly (from app code or each other)?</strong><=
/td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Yes (<code>CALL proc_name(...)</c=
ode>)</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Yes</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C No =E2=80=94 can't be invoked dir=
ectly</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Can be forgotten/skipped?</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F Yes =E2=80=94 only runs =
if someone remembers to call it</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F Yes =E2=80=94 only runs =
where it's used</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C No =E2=80=94 always runs, guarant=
eed</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Typical use case</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Reusable business logic, batch jobs, report=
ing</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Calculations, transformations</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Auditing, enforcing rules, keeping derived =
data in sync (auto-reactions to data changes)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<h4 id=3D"example--auditing-salary-changes">Example =E2=80=94 Auditing Sala=
ry Changes</h4>
<p>The same audit requirement as <a href=3D"#example-4--audit-log">Example =
4 =E2=80=94 Audit Log</a>, implemented both ways in MySQL to show the pract=
ical difference.</p>
<p><strong>Trigger (runs automatically, can't be bypassed):</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keywor=
d">TABLE</span> salary_audit (
    audit_id    <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span> AUTO_INCREMENT <span c=
lass=3D"hljs-keyword">PRIMARY</span> KEY,
    emp_id      <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span>,
    old_salary  <span class=3D"hljs-type">DECIMAL</span>(<span class=3D"hlj=
s-number">10</span>,<span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>),
    new_salary  <span class=3D"hljs-type">DECIMAL</span>(<span class=3D"hlj=
s-number">10</span>,<span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>),
    changed_at  DATETIME
);

DELIMITER $$
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">TRI=
GGER</span> trg_salary_audit
AFTER <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">UPDATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keywor=
d">ON</span> employees
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FOR</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">EACH</=
span> <span class=3D"hljs-type">ROW</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">BEGIN</span>
    IF OLD.salary <span class=3D"hljs-operator">&lt;&gt;</span> NEW.salary =
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">THEN</span>
        <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INSERT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyw=
ord">INTO</span> salary_audit (emp_id, old_salary, new_salary, changed_at)
        <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">VALUES</span> (OLD.emp_id, OLD.salary,=
 NEW.salary, NOW());
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">END</span> IF;
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">END</span>$$
DELIMITER ;

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Any UPDATE on employees.salary auto-logs it=
self =E2=80=94 no extra call needed:</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">UPDATE</span> employees <span class=3D"hljs-ke=
yword">SET</span> salary <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span cla=
ss=3D"hljs-number">75000</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> e=
mp_id <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-number">=
101</span>;</code></pre></div>
<p><strong>Stored Procedure (same result, but must be called explicitly):</=
strong></p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs">DELIMITER $$
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PRO=
CEDURE</span> update_salary(<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">IN</span> p_emp_id=
 <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">IN</spa=
n> p_new_salary <span class=3D"hljs-type">DECIMAL</span>(<span class=3D"hlj=
s-number">10</span>,<span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>))
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">BEGIN</span>
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">DECLARE</span> v_old_salary <span class=3D=
"hljs-type">DECIMAL</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-number">10</span>,<span clas=
s=3D"hljs-number">2</span>);

    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> salary <span class=3D"hljs-k=
eyword">INTO</span> v_old_salary <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FROM</span> e=
mployees <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> emp_id <span class=3D"hl=
js-operator">=3D</span> p_emp_id;
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">UPDATE</span> employees <span class=3D"hlj=
s-keyword">SET</span> salary <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> p_new=
_salary <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> emp_id <span class=3D"hlj=
s-operator">=3D</span> p_emp_id;

    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INSERT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword"=
>INTO</span> salary_audit (emp_id, old_salary, new_salary, changed_at)
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">VALUES</span> (p_emp_id, v_old_salary, p_n=
ew_salary, NOW());
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">END</span>$$
DELIMITER ;

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Must be called every time =E2=80=94 a plain=
 UPDATE bypasses it entirely:</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CALL</span> update_salary(<span class=3D"hljs-=
number">101</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">75000</span>);</code></pre>=
</div>
