<h3 id=3D"-why-do-most-companies-avoid-triggers--stored-procedures-and-keep=
-logic-in-the-application" data-toc=3D"Why Do Most Companies Avoid Triggers=
 &amp; Stored =E2=80=A6">=E2=9D=93 Why Do Most Companies Avoid Triggers &am=
p; Stored Procedures and Keep Logic in the Application?</h3>
<p>Triggers and stored procedures are powerful =E2=80=94 yet most modern pr=
oduct companies (especially at scale) deliberately keep business logic <str=
ong>in the application layer</strong> instead. Here's why.</p>
