</section><section class=3D"sec"><h2 id=3D"primary-key-vs-unique-key" data-=
toc=3D"16. Primary Key vs Unique Key"><span class=3D"sec-n">16.</span> Prim=
ary Key vs Unique Key</h2>
<p>Both Primary Key and Unique Key enforce <strong>uniqueness</strong>, but=
 they serve different purposes and have different rules. This is one of the=
 most frequently asked interview questions.</p>
<p>For the definitions, see <a href=3D"#3-primary-key">3. Primary Key</a> a=
nd <a href=3D"#4-alternate-key">4. Alternate Key</a> (an alternate key is e=
nforced with a <code>UNIQUE</code> constraint). This section compares the t=
wo directly.</p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"side-by-side-comparison-1" data-toc=3D"Side-by-Side Comparison">S=
ide-by-Side Comparison</h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Aspect</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Primary Key</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Unique Key</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Purpose</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Main identifier for the table</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Enforces uniqueness on additional columns (=
secondary identifier)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>NULL allowed?</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C Never (NOT NULL)</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Yes. MySQL, PostgreSQL and Oracle=
 allow <strong>multiple</strong> NULLs; SQL Server allows only <strong>one<=
/strong></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>How many per table?</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Only <strong>ONE</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>Multiple</strong> unique keys allow=
ed</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Creates index?</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Clustered index (by default)</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Non-clustered index</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Can be Foreign Key reference?</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Yes (most common)</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Yes (less common)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Auto NOT NULL?</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Automatically adds NOT NULL</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C Must specify NOT NULL explicitly<=
/td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Duplicate values?</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C Never</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C Never (except multiple NULLs, whe=
re the RDBMS allows them)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"example-3" data-toc=3D"Example">Example</h3>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keywor=
d">TABLE</span> employees (
    emp_id    <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyw=
ord">PRIMARY</span> KEY,           <span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- =E2=86=
=90 Only ONE primary key</span>
    email     <span class=3D"hljs-type">VARCHAR</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-=
number">100</span>) <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">UNIQUE</span>,       <span=
 class=3D"hljs-comment">-- =E2=86=90 Unique key #1</span>
    phone     <span class=3D"hljs-type">VARCHAR</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-=
number">15</span>) <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">UNIQUE</span>,        <span=
 class=3D"hljs-comment">-- =E2=86=90 Unique key #2</span>
    aadhar_no <span class=3D"hljs-type">VARCHAR</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-=
number">12</span>) <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">UNIQUE</span>,        <span=
 class=3D"hljs-comment">-- =E2=86=90 Unique key #3</span>
    name      <span class=3D"hljs-type">VARCHAR</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-=
number">50</span>),
    dept      <span class=3D"hljs-type">VARCHAR</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-=
number">50</span>)
);</code></pre></div>
