</section><section class=3D"sec"><h2 id=3D"uuid-vs-auto-increment-integer-a=
s-primary-key" data-toc=3D"17. UUID vs Auto-Increment Integer as Primary Ke=
y"><span class=3D"sec-n">17.</span> UUID vs Auto-Increment Integer as Prima=
ry Key</h2>
<p>Choosing between a UUID and an auto-increment integer (<code>INT</code>/=
<code>BIGINT</code>) as your primary key is one of the most impactful desig=
n decisions you'll make. It affects storage, query performance, insert thro=
ughput, index size, and how well your system scales across multiple databas=
es. Let's break it down.</p>
<p>=F0=9F=94=97 <a href=3D"https://planetscale.com/blog/the-problem-with-us=
ing-a-uuid-primary-key-in-mysql" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener">PlanetS=
cale =E2=80=94 The Problem with Using a UUID Primary Key in MySQL</a></p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"what-each-option-looks-like" data-toc=3D"What Each Option Looks L=
ike">What Each Option Looks Like</h3>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Auto-increment integer</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">TAB=
LE</span> orders (
    id <span class=3D"hljs-type">BIGINT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword"=
>PRIMARY</span> KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,    <span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- 1, 2=
, 3, 4, 5, ...</span>
    customer_id <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span>,
    total <span class=3D"hljs-type">DECIMAL</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-numb=
er">10</span>,<span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>)
);

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- UUID as CHAR(36)</span>
