0  then  501-1000  then  1001-1003, ...  where appends always land" title=
=3D"Auto-increment inserts 1001-1003 all append at the end of the B+ Tree; =
leaf pages  1-500  then  501-1000  then  1001-1003, ...  where appends alwa=
ys land" loading=3D"lazy"></figure>
<p><strong>Why this is fast:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>One hot page</strong> =E2=80=94 the rightmost leaf stays in the=
 buffer pool (memory). Writes hit RAM, not disk.</li>
<li><strong>No page splits in the middle</strong> =E2=80=94 splits only hap=
pen at the end, which is cheap.</li>
<li><strong>Sequential I/O</strong> =E2=80=94 if the page does need to be f=
lushed to disk, it's written sequentially (adjacent pages are next to each =
other on disk).</li>
<li><strong>Pages fill up to ~90-95%</strong> =E2=80=94 minimal wasted spac=
e because data is inserted in order.</li>
</ul>
<h4 id=3D"uuid-v4-random-inserts-slow">UUID (v4): Random Inserts (Slow)</h4=
>
<p>UUID v4 values are <strong>completely random</strong>: <code>a3b8d1b6...=
</code>, <code>f81d4fae...</code>, <code>0c8cfc82...</code>. Each new row's=
 key lands at a <strong>random position</strong> in the B+ Tree =E2=80=94 N=
