<h3 id=3D"other-prevention-techniques" data-toc=3D"Other Prevention Techniq=
ues">Other Prevention Techniques</h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Technique</th>
<th>How It Helps</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Parameterized queries</strong></td>
<td>Treats input as data, not SQL code (best defense)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Input validation</strong></td>
<td>Reject special characters (<code>'</code>, <code>&quot;</code>, <code>;=
</code>, <code>--</code>)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Stored procedures</strong></td>
<td>Precompiled SQL =E2=80=94 harder to inject</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Least privilege</strong></td>
<td>DB user should only have needed permissions (no DROP!)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>ORMs</strong></td>
<td>Frameworks like Hibernate, SQLAlchemy auto-parameterize</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>WAF (Web Application Firewall)</strong></td>
<td>Blocks common injection patterns</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Escape special characters</strong></td>
<td>Last resort =E2=80=94 less reliable than parameterization</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
