a.75.75 0 0 1-1.5 0v-2.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0ZM9 11a1 1 0 1 1-2 0 1 1 0 0 1 2=
 0Z"></path></svg>Warning</p><p><strong>MySQL has no user-name wildcard.</s=
trong> <code>'*'@'localhost'</code> is a user literally named <code>*</code=
>. The <code>%</code> wildcard works only in the <strong>host</strong> part=
 (<code>'Amit'@'%'</code> =3D Amit connecting from any host). To give many =
users the same rights, grant them to a <strong>role</strong> and assign tha=
t role to each user (MySQL 8.0+).</p>
</div>
