</section><section class=3D"sec"><h2 id=3D"indexes-in-mysql-innodb" data-to=
c=3D"20. Indexes in MySQL (InnoDB)"><span class=3D"sec-n">20.</span> Indexe=
s in MySQL (InnoDB)</h2>
<p>An index is a <strong>separate data structure</strong> that MySQL mainta=
ins alongside your table data. Its sole purpose is to make finding rows <st=
rong>fast</strong> =E2=80=94 without an index, MySQL has no choice but to s=
can every single row in the table (a &quot;full table scan&quot;) to answer=
 your query. With the right index, MySQL can jump directly to the matching =
rows, the same way a book's index lets you jump to the exact page instead o=
f reading the whole book.</p>
<p>Indexes are not free. They speed up reads but slow down writes, and they=
 consume storage. Understanding <strong>how</strong> they work internally i=
s the key to using them well.</p>
<p>=F0=9F=94=97 <a href=3D"https://planetscale.com/blog/how-do-database-ind=
exes-work" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener">PlanetScale =E2=80=94 How Do =
Database Indexes Work</a><br>
=F0=9F=94=97 <strong>Reference:</strong> <a href=3D"https://www.freecodecam=
p.org/news/database-indexing-at-a-glance-bb50809d48bd/" target=3D"_blank" r=
el=3D"noopener">freeCodeCamp =E2=80=94 Database Indexing at a Glance</a></p=
>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"what-is-an-index" data-toc=3D"What Is an Index?">What Is an Index=
?</h3>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note"><p class=3D"markdown-aler=
t-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-info mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" ver=
sion=3D"1.1" width=3D"16" height=3D"16" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M0 =
8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13=
ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 =
0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1=
 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z"></path></svg>Note</p><p><strong>Think of it this way:<=
/strong> A database without an index is like a book without a table of cont=
ents =E2=80=94 you'd have to read every page to find what you're looking fo=
r. An index is the table of contents that tells you exactly which page to g=
o to.</p>
</div>
