<h4 id=3D"secondary-index-any-non-primary-index">Secondary Index (Any Non-P=
rimary Index)</h4>
<p>A <strong>secondary (non-clustered) index</strong> is a <strong>separate=
 structure</strong> that stores the index key + a pointer back to the actua=
l data row. The table data stays in its own order (in InnoDB, primary key o=
rder) =E2=80=94 not the order of this index.</p>
