ding=3D"lazy"></figure>
<ul>
<li>There can be <strong>many</strong> per table</li>
<li>The leaf nodes store the <strong>indexed columns + the primary key valu=
e</strong> (NOT the full row) =E2=80=94 in InnoDB the PK value <em>is</em> =
the row pointer</li>
<li>Requires <strong>additional disk space</strong> for the index structure=
</li>
<li>To get columns not in the secondary index, InnoDB must do a <strong>sec=
ond lookup</strong> on the clustered index using the primary key =E2=80=94 =
this is called a <strong>bookmark lookup</strong> (or <strong>&quot;back to=
 table&quot;</strong>, sometimes called <strong>&quot;double lookup&quot;</=
strong>)</li>
</ul>
