<h4 id=3D"include-columns-mysql-80-functional-equivalent">INCLUDE Columns (=
MySQL 8.0+ Functional Equivalent)</h4>
<p>MySQL doesn't have a formal <code>INCLUDE</code> keyword (SQL Server/Pos=
tgreSQL do), but you can simulate it by adding columns to the end of a comp=
osite index. The extra columns are stored in the index but not used for sor=
ting =E2=80=94 they just &quot;come along for the ride&quot; to make the in=
dex covering.</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Make the index covering for queries t=
hat also need &#x27;name&#x27;</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> INDEX idx_dept_salary_name <span=
 class=3D"hljs-keyword">ON</span> employees (department, salary, name);

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Now this is a covering index:</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> department, salary, name <span c=
lass=3D"hljs-keyword">FROM</span> employees <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WH=
ERE</span> department <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=
=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;Engineering&#x27;</span>;</code></pre></div>
<p><strong>Trade-off:</strong> Wider indexes use more storage and are slowe=
r to maintain on writes. Only add columns to make an index covering if the =
query is critical and frequent.</p>
<h4 id=3D"how-to-know-if-your-query-uses-a-covering-index">How to Know if Y=
our Query Uses a Covering Index</h4>
<p>Run <code>EXPLAIN</code> and look at the <code>Extra</code> column:</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Extra Value</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>Using index</code></td>
<td>=E2=9C=85 Covering index =E2=80=94 data read from index only</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Using index condition</code></td>
<td>Index used for filtering, but table data still accessed</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>(nothing about index)</td>
<td>Index may or may not be used; table rows are being read</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
