<h4 id=3D"the-real-issue-is-selectivity">The Real Issue Is Selectivity</h4>
<p>Two terms that get confused:</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Term</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
<th>Formula</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Cardinality</strong></td>
<td>How many <strong>distinct</strong> values the column has</td>
<td><code>COUNT(DISTINCT col)</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Selectivity</strong></td>
<td>What fraction of the table one value narrows you down to</td>
<td><code>COUNT(DISTINCT col) / COUNT(*)</code></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
