<p>Two consequences people miss:</p>
<ul>
<li>Both pages are now ~50% full, so the <strong>table occupies roughly twi=
ce the disk</strong> for the same rows.</li>
<li>The split writes <strong>three</strong> dirty pages (old, new, parent) =
instead of one.</li>
</ul>
