<h4 id=3D"the-change-buffer--and-when-it-cant-save-you">The Change Buffer =
=E2=80=94 and When It Can't Save You</h4>
<p>To avoid a random disk read on every secondary index insert, InnoDB reco=
rds the change in the <strong>change buffer</strong> and merges it into the=
 real page later, when that page is read for some other reason (or by a bac=
kground merge). But it is <strong>not</strong> always available:</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Index being modified</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Change buffer usable?</th>
<th>Why</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Clustered index (PK)</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C No</td>
<td>The page is needed <em>right now</em> =E2=80=94 it's where the row is p=
hysically stored</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Secondary, non-unique</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Yes</td>
<td>Nothing needs checking, so the write can safely be deferred</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Secondary, UNIQUE</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C No</td>
<td>Uniqueness must be verified <em>immediately</em>, which forces the page=
 to be read from disk</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
