<h4 id=3D"-if-a-random-uuid-hurts-doesnt-an-index-on-email-hurt-too">=E2=9D=
=93 If a Random UUID Hurts, Doesn't an Index on <code>email</code> Hurt Too=
?</h4>
<p>A very fair question =E2=80=94 and the <strong>mechanism is identical</s=
trong>. Emails arrive in no order at all (<code>zoe@=E2=80=A6</code>, then =
<code>adam@=E2=80=A6</code>, then <code>mike@=E2=80=A6</code>), so every in=
sert lands at a random leaf of the email B+ Tree, causing the same page spl=
its and the same ~50% page fill.</p>
<p>So why does nobody worry about it? Because the <strong>blast radius</str=
ong> is completely different.</p>
