 0 0 1 0 2Z"></path></svg>Caution</p><p><strong>Never let a random value be=
 your clustered index. Anywhere else, randomness is a bounded, local cost y=
ou pay in exchange for a lookup you actually need.</strong></p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th></th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Random value OK?</th>
<th>Why</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>PRIMARY KEY</strong> (clustered)</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C <strong>No</strong></td>
<td>It dictates the physical order of your rows, and its size is copied int=
o every secondary index</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Secondary index / <code>UNIQUE</code> key</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 <strong>Yes</strong></td>
<td>It's just a side tree =E2=80=94 the cost is local, bounded, and undoabl=
e with one <code>DROP INDEX</code></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
</div>
<p>Every real schema has random-valued secondary indexes =E2=80=94 email, u=
sername, phone, external references, API keys. That is <strong>normal and c=
orrect</strong>. The problem was never &quot;random values in indexes&quot;=
; it was only ever &quot;random values in the <em>clustered</em> index.&quo=
t;</p>
<h5 id=3D"its-random-bad-not-uuid-bad">It's &quot;Random Bad&quot;, Not &qu=
ot;UUID Bad&quot;</h5>
<p>Not every UUID is random. Time-ordered IDs =E2=80=94 <strong>UUIDv7</str=
ong>, <strong>ULID</strong>, <strong>Snowflake</strong> =E2=80=94 are times=
tamp-prefixed, sort like an <code>AUTO_INCREMENT</code>, and are fine as a =
primary key; only fully random <strong>UUIDv4</strong> causes the problem. =
And if you're stuck with v4, keep a sequential <code>BIGINT</code> PK for s=
torage and expose the UUID through a <code>UNIQUE</code> secondary index, w=
here randomness is affordable.</p>
<p>=F0=9F=94=97 Full treatment in <a href=3D"#uuid-vs-auto-increment-intege=
r-as-primary-key">UUID vs Auto-Increment Integer as Primary Key</a> =E2=80=
=94 especially <a href=3D"#uuid-v7--ulid--the-best-of-both-worlds">UUID v7 =
/ ULID =E2=80=94 The Best of Both Worlds?</a> and <a href=3D"#best-practice=
-use-both-hybrid-approach">Best Practice: Use Both (Hybrid Approach)</a>.</=
p>
