<h4 id=3D"access-types-the-type-column--best-to-worst">Access Types (the <c=
ode>type</code> column) =E2=80=94 Best to Worst</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Type</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
<th>Performance</th>
<th>Example</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>system</code></td>
<td>Table has exactly 1 row</td>
<td>=E2=9A=A1 Best</td>
<td>System tables</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>const</code></td>
<td>At most 1 matching row (unique index + constant)</td>
<td>=E2=9A=A1 Excellent</td>
<td><code>WHERE id =3D 42</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>eq_ref</code></td>
<td>1 matching row per join iteration (unique index)</td>
<td>=E2=9A=A1 Excellent</td>
<td><code>JOIN ON pk =3D fk</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>ref</code></td>
<td>Multiple matching rows via non-unique index</td>
<td>=E2=9C=85 Good</td>
<td><code>WHERE customer_id =3D 42</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>range</code></td>
<td>Index range scan</td>
<td>=E2=9C=85 Good</td>
<td><code>WHERE created_at &gt;=3D '2026-09-01'</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>index</code></td>
<td>Full index scan (reads entire index, not table)</td>
<td>=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F Okay</td>
<td>Covering index on <code>SELECT col</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>ALL</code></td>
<td><strong>Full table scan</strong> =E2=80=94 no index used</td>
<td>=F0=9F=94=B4 Bad</td>
<td><code>WHERE func(col) =3D val</code></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p><strong>Goal:</strong> Get your important queries to <code>const</code>,=
 <code>eq_ref</code>, <code>ref</code>, or <code>range</code>. If <code>EXP=
LAIN</code> shows <code>ALL</code> for a large table, that query needs an i=
ndex.</p>
<h4 id=3D"important-extra-values">Important <code>Extra</code> Values</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Extra Value</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
<th>Action</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>Using index</code></td>
<td>=E2=9C=85 Covering index =E2=80=94 data read from index only</td>
<td>Great =E2=80=94 no table access needed</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Using where</code></td>
<td>Filtering happens after reading (normal)</td>
<td>Fine =E2=80=94 check if an index could push filtering earlier</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Using index condition</code></td>
<td>Index Condition Pushdown (ICP) =E2=80=94 filtering pushed to storage en=
gine level</td>
<td>Good optimization</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Backward index scan</code></td>
<td>=E2=9C=85 Index read in reverse order to satisfy <code>ORDER BY =E2=80=
=A6 DESC</code> (MySQL 8.0)</td>
<td>Fine =E2=80=94 no sort needed</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Using temporary</code></td>
<td>=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F MySQL created a temporary table (for GROUP BY, DISTI=
NCT, ORDER BY)</td>
<td>Consider adding an index to avoid this</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Using filesort</code></td>
<td>=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F MySQL sorted results in memory/on disk instead of us=
ing an index</td>
<td>Add an index matching the ORDER BY</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Using join buffer (hash join)</code></td>
<td>=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F No index for the join =E2=80=94 MySQL builds an in-m=
emory hash table (8.0.18+; older versions say <code>Block Nested Loop</code=
>)</td>
<td>Add an index on the join column</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Select tables optimized away</code></td>
<td>=E2=9C=85 Query answered from index metadata alone (e.g., <code>MIN</co=
de>/<code>MAX</code>)</td>
<td>Best possible case</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
