+------+----------------------+---------+-------+------+-------------+</cod=
e></pre></div>
<p>=E2=9C=85 Every column the query needs (<code>customer_id</code>, <code>=
status</code>, <code>created_at</code>) is inside <code>idx_cust_status_dat=
e</code>, so MySQL never touches the table rows. See <a href=3D"#covering-i=
ndexes-and-index-only-scans">Covering Indexes</a>.</p>
<p><strong>Scenario 6 =E2=80=94 A JOIN: multiple rows, read top to bottom</=
strong></p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> INDEX idx_created <span cl=
ass=3D"hljs-keyword">ON</span> orders (created_at);

EXPLAIN
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> c.name, o.id, o.total_amount
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FROM</span>   orders o
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">JOIN</span>   customers c <span class=3D"hljs-=
keyword">ON</span> c.id <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> o.customer=
_id
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span>  o.created_at <span class=3D"hljs=
-operator">&gt;=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;2026-09-01&#x27=
;</span>
  <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">AND</span>  o.status <span class=3D"hljs-ope=
rator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;SHIPPED&#x27;</span>\G<=
/code></pre></div>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">text</span></div><pre><code class=3D=
"hljs">*************************** 1. row ***************************
           id: 1
  select_type: SIMPLE
        table: o
   partitions: NULL
         type: range
possible_keys: idx_cust_status_date,idx_cust_date,idx_created
          key: idx_created
      key_len: 5
          ref: NULL
         rows: 5434
     filtered: 20.00
        Extra: Using where
*************************** 2. row ***************************
           id: 1
  select_type: SIMPLE
        table: c
   partitions: NULL
         type: eq_ref
possible_keys: PRIMARY
          key: PRIMARY
      key_len: 4
          ref: shop.o.customer_id
         rows: 1
     filtered: 100.00
        Extra: NULL
2 rows in set, 1 warning (0.00 sec)</code></pre></div>
<p>How to read it:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Same <code>id</code> (1) =E2=86=92 one nested-loop join.</stron=
g> The first row (<code>o</code>) is the <strong>outer / driving</strong> t=
able; for each of its rows MySQL looks up the second (<code>c</code>).</li>
<li><strong><code>o</code>: <code>range</code> on <code>idx_created</code><=
/strong> =E2=86=92 reads ~5,434 orders since 1 Sep. <code>filtered =3D 20.0=
0</code> =E2=86=92 about 20% are <code>SHIPPED</code>, so ~<strong>1,087</s=
trong> rows go on to the join (<code>5434 =C3=97 20%</code>).</li>
<li><strong><code>c</code>: <code>eq_ref</code> on <code>PRIMARY</code></st=
rong> with <code>ref =3D shop.o.customer_id</code> =E2=86=92 exactly <stron=
g>1</strong> customer per order, by primary key. Best possible join access.=
</li>
<li><strong>Total work =E2=89=88 5,434 index reads + ~1,087 PK lookups.</st=
rong> Multiply <code>rows =C3=97 filtered</code> down the list to estimate =
it.</li>
</ol>
<p>=F0=9F=94=8D Could it be better? <code>status</code> is filtered <em>aft=
er</em> the range read (<code>Using where</code>). An index on <code>(statu=
s, created_at)</code> would let MySQL read only <code>SHIPPED</code> rows f=
rom 1 Sep onward. <code>EXPLAIN ANALYZE</code> (next) tells you whether tha=
t's worth it.</p>
<h4 id=3D"explain-analyze--reading-the-tree">EXPLAIN ANALYZE =E2=80=94 Read=
ing the Tree</h4>
<p><code>EXPLAIN ANALYZE</code> prints the plan as a tree and annotates eve=
ry node with <strong>estimates</strong> and <strong>actuals</strong>:</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">text</span></div><pre><code class=3D=
"hljs">-&gt; Node description  (cost=3DC rows=3DR_est) (actual time=3DFIRST=
..LAST rows=3DR_act loops=3DL)</code></pre></div>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Part</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Indentation</strong></td>
<td>Children run first and feed their rows to the parent. Read <strong>from=
 the most-indented line outward</strong></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>cost=3D</code></td>
<td>Optimizer's estimated cost =E2=80=94 abstract units, <strong>not</stron=
g> milliseconds</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>rows=3D</code> (1st)</td>
<td><strong>Estimated</strong> rows this node returns</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>actual time=3DFIRST..LAST</code></td>
<td>Milliseconds to the <strong>first</strong> row and to the <strong>last<=
/strong> row, <strong>per loop</strong></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>rows=3D</code> (2nd)</td>
<td><strong>Actual</strong> rows returned, <strong>per loop</strong></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>loops=3D</code></td>
<td>How many times the node ran (inner side of a join runs once per outer r=
ow)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-important"><p class=3D"markdown=
-alert-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-report mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 =
16" version=3D"1.1" width=3D"16" height=3D"16" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=
