</section><section class=3D"sec"><h2 id=3D"functional-dependencies-in-dbms"=
 data-toc=3D"23. Functional Dependencies in DBMS"><span class=3D"sec-n">23.=
</span> Functional Dependencies in DBMS</h2>
<p>A <strong>functional dependency (FD)</strong> describes a relationship b=
etween attributes in a table where one attribute (or set of attributes) <st=
rong>uniquely determines</strong> another attribute.</p>
<p><strong>Notation:</strong> <code>X =E2=86=92 Y</code> means &quot;X func=
tionally determines Y&quot; =E2=80=94 if you know X, you can determine exac=
tly one value of Y.</p>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note"><p class=3D"markdown-aler=
t-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-info mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" ver=
sion=3D"1.1" width=3D"16" height=3D"16" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M0 =
8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13=
ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 =
0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1=
 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z"></path></svg>Note</p><p><strong>Think of it this way:<=
/strong> If you know a student's <code>roll_no</code>, you can determine th=
eir <code>name</code>. So <code>roll_no =E2=86=92 name</code>. But knowing =
the <code>name</code> doesn't tell you the <code>roll_no</code> (names can =
repeat). So <code>name =E2=86=92 roll_no</code> is NOT a valid FD.</p>
</div>
