 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z"></path></svg>Note</p><p><strong>Think of it as:</stron=
g> &quot;If you know someone's full name, you obviously know their first na=
me.&quot; That's trivially true.</p>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"rule-x--y-is-trivial-if-y--x">Rule: <code>X =E2=86=92 Y</code> is=
 trivial if <code>Y =E2=8A=86 X</code></h4>
<h4 id=3D"examples-3">Examples</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Dependency</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Trivial?</th>
<th>Why</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>{roll_no, name} =E2=86=92 name</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Trivial</td>
<td><code>name</code> is already in <code>{roll_no, name}</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>{roll_no, name} =E2=86=92 roll_no</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Trivial</td>
<td><code>roll_no</code> is already in <code>{roll_no, name}</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>{roll_no} =E2=86=92 roll_no</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Trivial</td>
<td>Same attribute on both sides</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>{roll_no, course_id} =E2=86=92 roll_no</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Trivial</td>
<td><code>roll_no</code> is a subset of the left side</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
