_head</code> is stored only ONCE per department =E2=80=94 worked through wi=
th tables and SQL in <a href=3D"#3nf--third-normal-form">3NF =E2=80=94 Thir=
d Normal Form</a>.</p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"all-5-types-at-a-glance" data-toc=3D"All 5 Types at a Glance">All=
 5 Types at a Glance</h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Type</th>
<th>Rule</th>
<th>Example</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Useful?</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Trivial</strong></td>
<td><code>Y =E2=8A=86 X</code></td>
<td><code>{roll_no, name} =E2=86=92 name</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C Obvious, useless</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Non-Trivial</strong></td>
<td><code>Y =E2=8A=84 X</code></td>
<td><code>roll_no =E2=86=92 name</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Meaningful</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Full</strong></td>
<td>No subset of X can determine Y</td>
<td><code>{roll_no, course_id} =E2=86=92 grade</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Required for 2NF</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Partial</strong></td>
<td>A subset of X can determine Y</td>
<td><code>{roll_no, course_id} =E2=86=92 name</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C Causes redundancy</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Transitive</strong></td>
<td><code>X =E2=86=92 Y =E2=86=92 Z</code> (Y =E2=86=9B X)</td>
<td><code>roll_no =E2=86=92 dept =E2=86=92 dept_head</code></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C Causes redundancy</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"connection-to-normalization" data-toc=3D"Connection to Normalizat=
ion">Connection to Normalization</h3>
<p>Each normal form forbids one more kind of dependency: <strong>2NF</stron=
g> removes partial FDs, <strong>3NF</strong> removes transitive FDs, and <s=
trong>BCNF</strong> forbids any non-trivial FD whose left side is not a sup=
er key. The full ladder is in <a href=3D"#the-ladder-of-normal-forms">The L=
adder of Normal Forms</a>.</p>
