</section><section class=3D"sec"><h2 id=3D"database-anomalies" data-toc=3D"=
24. Database Anomalies"><span class=3D"sec-n">24.</span> Database Anomalies=
</h2>
<p>Anomalies are <strong>problems that arise when a database table is not p=
roperly normalized</strong>. They occur because of <strong>redundant data</=
strong> =E2=80=94 the same piece of information is stored in multiple rows.=
 When you try to insert, delete, or update data in such a table, you run in=
to inconsistencies.</p>
<p>There are <strong>three types</strong> of anomalies: <strong>Insertion</=
strong>, <strong>Deletion</strong>, and <strong>Update</strong>.</p>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note"><p class=3D"markdown-aler=
t-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-info mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" ver=
sion=3D"1.1" width=3D"16" height=3D"16" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M0 =
8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13=
