"M6.457 1.047c.659-1.234 2.427-1.234 3.086 0l6.082 11.378A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 1=
4.082 15H1.918a1.75 1.75 0 0 1-1.543-2.575Zm1.763.707a.25.25 0 0 0-.44 0L1.=
698 13.132a.25.25 0 0 0 .22.368h12.164a.25.25 0 0 0 .22-.368Zm.53 3.996v2.5=
a.75.75 0 0 1-1.5 0v-2.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0ZM9 11a1 1 0 1 1-2 0 1 1 0 0 1 2=
 0Z"></path></svg>Warning</p><p><strong>Problem:</strong> Updating a piece =
of data requires changing it in <strong>multiple rows</strong>. If you miss=
 even one row, the database becomes <strong>inconsistent</strong> =E2=80=94=
 it now holds <strong>two contradictory versions of one truth</strong>.</p>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"example-6">Example</h4>
<p>Suppose <strong>Dr. Gupta retires</strong> and <strong>Dr. Mehta</strong=
> becomes the new head of Computer Science. You need to update every row wh=
ere <code>Department =3D 'Computer Science'</code>:</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
