for interviews:</strong> &quot;Normalization is a step-by-step decompositio=
n of tables, driven by functional dependencies, to remove redundancy and in=
sert/update/delete anomalies =E2=80=94 each normal form is a stricter rule =
about which dependencies are allowed to survive.&quot;</p>
</div>
<p>It was introduced by <strong>E. F. Codd</strong> (1NF/2NF/3NF in 1970=E2=
=80=9372) and refined into <strong>BCNF</strong> by Codd and Boyce (1974). =
Higher forms (4NF, 5NF) exist for multivalued and join dependencies, but re=
al-world schemas are designed to <strong>3NF</strong>, occasionally <strong=
>BCNF</strong> =E2=80=94 which is where this section stops.</p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"why-normalize--the-three-anomalies" data-toc=3D"Why Normalize? =
=E2=80=94 The Three Anomalies">Why Normalize? =E2=80=94 The Three Anomalies=
</h3>
