<h4 id=3D"benefits-vs-costs">Benefits vs Costs</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>=E2=9C=85 Benefits of normalizing</th>
<th>=E2=9D=8C Costs of normalizing</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Less redundancy =E2=86=92 smaller storage</td>
<td>More tables =E2=86=92 more <strong>JOINs</strong> per read query</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>No insert/update/delete anomalies</td>
<td>Reads can get slower (join cost)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Each fact updated in one place =E2=86=92 consistency</td>
<td>More complex queries to write</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Cleaner schema, easier to extend</td>
<td>Reporting/analytics queries may need denormalized copies</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"the-ladder-of-normal-forms" data-toc=3D"The Ladder of Normal Form=
s">The Ladder of Normal Forms</h3>
