<hr>
<h3 id=3D"1nf--first-normal-form" data-toc=3D"1NF =E2=80=94 First Normal Fo=
rm">1NF =E2=80=94 First Normal Form</h3>
<p><strong>Rule:</strong> every attribute must be <strong>atomic</strong> (=
single-valued and indivisible), each column must hold one data type, and th=
ere must be <strong>no repeating groups</strong> or arrays inside a cell. R=
ow order and column order must carry no meaning.</p>
<h4 id=3D"-violates-1nf">=E2=9D=8C Violates 1NF</h4>
<p><code>phone</code> stores two numbers in one cell:</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">roll_no</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">student_name</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:left">phone</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">1</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Alice</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:left">9990001111, 9990002222</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">2</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Bob</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:left">8880003333</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p><strong>Why it's a problem:</strong> you can't index or search a single =
phone efficiently, <code>WHERE phone =3D '9990002222'</code> needs string m=
atching, and adding/removing one number means rewriting the whole cell.</p>
<h4 id=3D"the-other-bad-fix--repeating-columns">The other bad &quot;fix&quo=
t; =E2=80=94 repeating columns</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">roll_no</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">student_name</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">phone1</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">phone2</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">phone3</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">1</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Alice</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">9990001111</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">9990002222</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">NULL</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>This is still wrong: it caps how many phones a student can have and fill=
s the table with NULLs. <strong>Repeating groups (<code>phone1..phoneN</cod=
e>) are a 1NF violation, not a solution.</strong></p>
<h4 id=3D"-in-1nf--one-row-per-value">=E2=9C=85 In 1NF =E2=80=94 one row pe=
r value</h4>
<p><strong><code>students</code></strong></p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">roll_no (PK)</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">student_name</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">1</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Alice</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">2</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Bob</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p><strong><code>student_phones</code></strong></p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">roll_no (PK, FK)</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">phone (PK)</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">1</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">9990001111</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">1</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">9990002222</td>
</tr>
<tr>
