<h3 id=3D"bcnf--boycecodd-normal-form-35nf" data-toc=3D"BCNF =E2=80=94 Boyc=
e=E2=80=93Codd Normal Form (3.5NF)">BCNF =E2=80=94 Boyce=E2=80=93Codd Norma=
l Form (3.5NF)</h3>
<p><strong>Rule:</strong> for <strong>every</strong> non-trivial functional=
 dependency <code>X =E2=86=92 Y</code>, <strong>X must be a super key</stro=
ng>. BCNF is 3NF <em>without</em> the escape clause &quot;=E2=80=A6or Y is =
a prime attribute&quot; =E2=80=94 so it is strictly stronger.</p>
<p>BCNF only differs from 3NF when a table has <strong>multiple overlapping=
 candidate keys</strong>.</p>
