<p><strong>Why it's in 3NF:</strong> in <code>teacher =E2=86=92 subject</co=
de>, the right-hand side <code>subject</code> <em>is</em> a prime attribute=
, so 3NF's escape clause is satisfied.
<strong>Why it fails BCNF:</strong> the determinant <code>teacher</code> is=
 not a super key.</p>
<p><strong>The anomaly that survives 3NF:</strong> you cannot record that <=
code>Dr. Kumar</code> teaches <code>Networks</code> until some student take=
s it, and if <code>Dr. Smith</code> switches to <code>Compilers</code> you =
must update multiple rows.</p>
