<h3 id=3D"two-rules-every-decomposition-must-respect" data-toc=3D"Two Rules=
 Every Decomposition Must Respect">Two Rules Every Decomposition Must Respe=
ct</h3>
<p>When you split a table <code>R</code> into <code>R1</code> and <code>R2<=
/code>, check both properties:</p>
<h4 id=3D"1-lossless-join-mandatory">1. Lossless Join (mandatory)</h4>
<p><code>R1 =E2=8B=88 R2</code> must give back <strong>exactly</strong> <co=
de>R</code> =E2=80=94 no lost rows, no spurious extra rows.</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">text</span></div><pre><code class=3D=
"hljs">  Condition:  attributes(R1) =E2=88=A9 attributes(R2)  must contain =
a
              super key of R1 or of R2</code></pre></div>
<p><strong>Lossy example:</strong> splitting <code>student_report(roll_no, =
course_id, marks)</code> into <code>(roll_no, marks)</code> and <code>(cour=
se_id, marks)</code> and joining on <code>marks</code> produces garbage row=
s =E2=80=94 <code>marks</code> is not a key of either part.</p>
<h4 id=3D"2-dependency-preservation-desirable">2. Dependency Preservation (=
desirable)</h4>
<p>Every FD of <code>R</code> should be checkable inside <strong>one</stron=
g> of the decomposed tables, without needing a join. If not, the constraint=
 has to move into application logic or a trigger.</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Property</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">3NF</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">BCNF</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Lossless join</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Always</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Always</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Dependency preservation</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Always</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F Not guaranteed</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
