inal 3NF schema: departments 1=E2=80=93N students 1=E2=80=93N student_phone=
s; students 1=E2=80=93N enrollment; enrollment N=E2=80=931 courses" title=
=3D"Final 3NF schema: departments 1=E2=80=93N students 1=E2=80=93N student_=
phones; students 1=E2=80=93N enrollment; enrollment N=E2=80=931 courses" lo=
ading=3D"lazy"></figure>
<p>Every fact now lives in exactly one place: a student's name in <code>stu=
dents</code>, a course's title in <code>courses</code>, a department's head=
 in <code>departments</code>, and a grade in <code>enrollment</code>.</p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"anomalies-resolved-by-normalization--deep-dive" data-toc=3D"Anoma=
lies Resolved by Normalization =E2=80=94 Deep Dive">Anomalies Resolved by N=
ormalization =E2=80=94 Deep Dive</h3>
<p>=F0=9F=94=97 <strong>Reference:</strong> <a href=3D"https://dba.stackexc=
hange.com/questions/194631/how-does-normalization-fix-the-three-types-of-up=
date-anomalies" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener">DBA StackExchange =E2=80=
=94 How does normalization fix the three types of update anomalies?</a></p>
<p>The three anomalies are defined in <a href=3D"#database-anomalies">Datab=
ase Anomalies</a>. Here they are on the <code>student_report</code> table f=
rom <a href=3D"#why-normalize--the-three-anomalies">Why Normalize?</a> =E2=
=80=94 PK <code>{roll_no, course_id}</code>, ignoring the <code>phone</code=
> column (split out in 1NF) =E2=80=94 together with how the 3NF schema abov=
e removes each one.</p>
<p>The key insight: <strong>normalization does not &quot;detect and repair&=
quot; anomalies at runtime.</strong> It restructures the schema so that eac=
h fact has exactly <strong>one</strong> home, which makes the anomaly <em>s=
tructurally impossible</em> =E2=80=94 and turns the rule into a <strong>key=
 constraint the DBMS itself enforces</strong>, instead of a convention your=
 application code has to remember.</p>
<hr>
<h4 id=3D"1-fixing-the-insertion-anomaly">1. Fixing the Insertion Anomaly</=
h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Scenario</th>
<th>What blocks you</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Add a new course <code>C4 =E2=80=94 Compilers</code> that nobody has en=
rolled in yet</td>
<td>The PK requires <code>roll_no</code>, so there's no legal row for a cou=
rse by itself</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Register a new department <code>MECH</code> with head <code>Dr. Iyer</c=
ode></td>
<td>You need at least one student in <code>MECH</code> first</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Admit a student who hasn't picked courses yet</td>
<td><code>course_id</code> is part of the PK and cannot be NULL</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- =E2=9D=8C Impossible on the unnormali=
zed table: no student, no row</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INSERT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INT=
O</span> student_report (course_id, course_name) <span class=3D"hljs-keywor=
d">VALUES</span> (<span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;C4&#x27;</span>, <span =
class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;Compilers&#x27;</span>);
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">--   ERROR: Column &#x27;roll_no&#x27; cannot =
be null (part of the primary key)</span>

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- The ugly workaround people reach for =E2=80=
=94 a fake placeholder row:</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INSERT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INT=
O</span> student_report <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">VALUES</span> (<span c=
lass=3D"hljs-keyword">NULL</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">NULL</span>=
, <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;C4&#x27;</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-st=
ring">&#x27;Compilers&#x27;</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">NULL</span=
>, <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">NULL</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">N=
ULL</span>);
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">--   Illegal (PK can&#x27;t be NULL), and poll=
utes the table if forced through</span></code></pre></div>
<p><strong>=E2=9C=85 How normalization fixes it =E2=80=94 2NF/3NF give each=
 entity its own table:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INSERT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keywor=
d">INTO</span> courses     <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">VALUES</span> (<spa=
n class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;C4&#x27;</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">=
&#x27;Compilers&#x27;</span>);        <span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- cours=
e exists on its own</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INSERT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INT=
O</span> departments <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">VALUES</span> (<span clas=
s=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;MECH&#x27;</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x2=
7;Dr. Iyer&#x27;</span>);       <span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- department =
exists on its own</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INSERT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INT=
O</span> students    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">VALUES</span> (<span clas=
s=3D"hljs-number">4</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;Dave&#x27;</s=
pan>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;MECH&#x27;</span>);        <span cl=
ass=3D"hljs-comment">-- student with no enrolments yet</span></code></pre><=
/div>
<p><strong>Why it works:</strong> an <em>independent entity</em> now has an=
 <em>independent table</em> with its own primary key, so its existence no l=
onger depends on a related row existing.</p>
<hr>
<h4 id=3D"2-fixing-the-deletion-anomaly">2. Fixing the Deletion Anomaly</h4=
>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Scenario</th>
<th>Collateral damage</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Bob drops course <code>C1</code> (his only enrolment)</td>
<td>You also lose &quot;Bob is a student&quot; <strong>and</strong> &quot;E=
CE's head is Dr. Jones&quot;</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Course <code>C3</code> is discontinued</td>
<td>You lose the fact that Carol is a student in CSE</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Last CSE student graduates</td>
<td>The CSE department vanishes from the database</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- =E2=9D=8C Intent: &quot;Bob dropped o=
ne course.&quot;  Actual effect: Bob and ECE cease to exist.</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">DELETE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FRO=
M</span> student_report <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> roll_no <=
span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span=
> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">AND</span> course_id <span class=3D"hljs-ope=
rator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;C1&#x27;</span>;</code>=
</pre></div>
<p><strong>=E2=9C=85 How normalization fixes it =E2=80=94 separate lifetime=
s, separate tables:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Intent maps exactly to one table; not=
hing else is touched</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">DELETE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FRO=
M</span> enrollment <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> roll_no <span=
 class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span> <s=
pan class=3D"hljs-keyword">AND</span> course_id <span class=3D"hljs-operato=
r">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;C1&#x27;</span>;

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- students(2, &#x27;Bob&#x27;, &#x27;ECE&#x27=
;)          =E2=86=92 still there =E2=9C=85</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- departments(&#x27;ECE&#x27;, &#x27;Dr. Jone=
s&#x27;)    =E2=86=92 still there =E2=9C=85</span></code></pre></div>
<p><strong>Why it works:</strong> each table now models one entity with its=
 <strong>own lifecycle</strong>. Removing an enrolment removes only the enr=
olment. Foreign keys with <code>ON DELETE RESTRICT</code> / <code>CASCADE</=
code> then let you state deliberately what <em>should</em> cascade =E2=80=
=94 instead of losing data by accident.</p>
<hr>
<h4 id=3D"3-fixing-the-modification-update-anomaly">3. Fixing the Modificat=
ion (Update) Anomaly</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Scenario</th>
<th>Rows that must all change together</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Rename course <code>DBMS</code> =E2=86=92 <code>Database Systems</code>=
</td>
<td>Every enrolment row for <code>C1</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>CSE's head changes to <code>Dr. Nair</code></td>
<td>Every row of every CSE student</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Alice's name is corrected to <code>Alicia</code></td>
<td>Every enrolment row for <code>roll_no =3D 1</code></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- =E2=9D=8C On the unnormalized table t=
his MUST hit every matching row</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">UPDATE</span> student_report <span class=3D"hl=
js-keyword">SET</span> dept_head <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <=
span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;Dr. Nair&#x27;</span> <span class=3D"hljs-=
keyword">WHERE</span> dept <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span c=
lass=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;CSE&#x27;</span>;</code></pre></div>
<p>If that statement is filtered wrongly, interrupted, or run as several st=
atements and one fails, you get:</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">roll_no</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">dept</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">dept_head</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">1</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">CSE</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Dr. Nair</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">3</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">CSE</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Dr. Smith</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>Nothing in the schema forbids this state: <code>dept_head</code> is not =
determined by any key, so the DBMS has no basis to reject it.</p>
<p><strong>=E2=9C=85 How normalization fixes it =E2=80=94 3NF puts the fact=
 in one row:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">UPDATE</span> departments <span class=3D=
"hljs-keyword">SET</span> dept_head <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span=
> <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;Dr. Nair&#x27;</span> <span class=3D"hl=
js-keyword">WHERE</span> dept <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <spa=
n class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;CSE&#x27;</span>;   <span class=3D"hljs-comme=
nt">-- exactly 1 row</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">UPDATE</span> courses     <span class=3D"hljs-=
keyword">SET</span> course_name <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <s=
pan class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;Database Systems&#x27;</span> <span class=
=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> course_id <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D<=
/span> <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;C1&#x27;</span>;
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">UPDATE</span> students    <span class=3D"hljs-=
keyword">SET</span> student_name <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <=
span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;Alicia&#x27;</span> <span class=3D"hljs-ke=
yword">WHERE</span> roll_no <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span =
class=3D"hljs-number">1</span>;</code></pre></div>
<p><strong>Why it works:</strong> a single-row update is <strong>atomic by =
construction</strong> =E2=80=94 there is no second copy left behind to disa=
gree with. Partial-update inconsistency becomes unrepresentable.</p>
<hr>
<h4 id=3D"which-normal-form-fixes-which-anomaly">Which Normal Form Fixes Wh=
ich Anomaly?</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Normal Form</th>
<th>Dependency removed</th>
<th>Anomalies it eliminates</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>1NF</strong></td>
<td>Multi-valued cells / repeating groups</td>
<td>Can't insert, search, or delete an individual value inside a cell</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>2NF</strong></td>
<td><strong>Partial</strong> (<code>part-of-key =E2=86=92 non-key</code>)</=
td>
<td>Course/student facts duplicated per enrolment =E2=80=94 insert a course=
 with no students; rename a course once</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>3NF</strong></td>
<td><strong>Transitive</strong> (<code>non-key =E2=86=92 non-key</code>)</t=
d>
<td>Department facts duplicated per student =E2=80=94 register a department=
 with no students; change its head once; keep it when the last student leav=
es</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>BCNF</strong></td>
<td>Any FD whose LHS isn't a super key</td>
<td>Residual anomalies when candidate keys overlap (e.g. record a teacher's=
 subject before any student enrols)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<hr>
<h4 id=3D"before--after-side-by-side">Before =E2=9E=9C After, Side by Side<=
/h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Operation</th>
<th>Unnormalized <code>student_report</code></th>
<th>Normalized (3NF) schema</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Add a course nobody takes</td>
<td>=E2=9D=8C Impossible (PK needs <code>roll_no</code>)</td>
<td>=E2=9C=85 1 <code>INSERT</code> into <code>courses</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Add a department with no students</td>
<td>=E2=9D=8C Impossible</td>
<td>=E2=9C=85 1 <code>INSERT</code> into <code>departments</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Rename a course</td>
<td>=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F N rows; partial failure =E2=87=92 inconsistency</td>
<td>=E2=9C=85 1 row in <code>courses</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Change a department head</td>
<td>=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F N rows; partial failure =E2=87=92 inconsistency</td>
<td>=E2=9C=85 1 row in <code>departments</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Student drops one course</td>
<td>=E2=9D=8C May delete the student and the department too</td>
<td>=E2=9C=85 1 <code>DELETE</code> from <code>enrollment</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Who enforces the rule?</td>
<td>=F0=9F=99=8B Application code / developer discipline</td>
<td>=F0=9F=94=92 The DBMS, via primary and foreign keys</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-important"><p class=3D"markdown=
-alert-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-report mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 =
