<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">State</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>Active</strong></td>
<td>Transaction is executing. Initial state of every transaction.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>Partially Committed</strong></td>
<td>Final operation has been executed, but not yet written to disk permanen=
tly.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>Committed</strong></td>
<td>All changes are permanently saved. Transaction is complete. =E2=9C=85</=
td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>Failed</strong></td>
<td>An error or check failure occurs. Transaction cannot proceed.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>Aborted</strong></td>
<td>All changes are rolled back. Database restored to pre-transaction state=
. After abort: restart or kill.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>Terminated</strong></td>
<td>The final state. The transaction has left the system =E2=80=94 reached =
either via <strong>Committed</strong> or via <strong>Aborted</strong> (and =
then killed rather than restarted).</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
