 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z"></path></svg>Note</p><p><strong>Why &quot;Terminated&q=
uot; matters:</strong> it's the single exit state of the lifecycle. <code>C=
ommitted =E2=86=92 Terminated</code> is the happy path; <code>Aborted =E2=
=86=92 Terminated</code> is the give-up path. A restarted transaction is a =
<strong>brand-new</strong> transaction, not a continuation of the aborted o=
ne.</p>
