 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z"></path></svg>Note</p><p><strong>After COMMIT:</strong>=
 Changes are permanent. Even if the system crashes right after, the data is=
 safe.
Strictly, what reaches disk at <code>COMMIT</code> is the <strong>redo log =
record</strong> (<code>fsync</code>ed); the table pages themselves are writ=
ten later in the background, and the log is replayed if a crash happens fir=
st. See <a href=3D"#durability-in-databases">Durability in Databases</a>.</=
p>
