during the transaction; COMMIT swings it to the new copy (old deleted), fai=
lure keeps the original (new copy deleted)" title=3D"Shadow copy: db-pointe=
r stays on the original during the transaction; COMMIT swings it to the new=
 copy (old deleted), failure keeps the original (new copy deleted)" loading=
=3D"lazy"></figure>
<p><strong>How it works:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Before modifying anything, create a <strong>complete copy</strong> of t=
he database</li>
<li>Apply all changes to the <strong>new copy only</strong> =E2=80=94 origi=
nal (shadow) is untouched</li>
<li><strong>On COMMIT:</strong> Update <code>db-pointer</code> to point to =
the new copy =E2=86=92 atomic switch</li>
<li><strong>On FAILURE:</strong> Delete the new copy =E2=86=92 original is =
still intact</li>
</ol>
