<h3 id=3D"4-durability--how-its-achieved" data-toc=3D"4. Durability =E2=80=
=94 How It's Achieved">4. Durability =E2=80=94 How It's Achieved</h3>
<p>Durability is achieved with <strong>Write-Ahead Logging (WAL) + a redo l=
og</strong>: every change is written to a durable log on disk before <code>=
COMMIT</code> returns, and replayed after a crash. Full walkthrough (commit=
 path, crash at every point, recovery with REDO/UNDO, <code>fsync</code>, c=
heckpoints, doublewrite, replication): <a href=3D"#durability-in-databases"=
>Durability in Databases</a>.</p>
