<p>So you'd write ~16 KB per page just to change a few bytes, and seek to r=
andom places on the disk to do it.</p>
<p><strong>3. Deferring lets the DB batch many changes into one write</stro=
ng> (<strong>write coalescing</strong>).
A hot page (a popular product's stock row, or the last page of an auto-incr=
ement index) may be modified 1,000 times in a minute.</p>
