<p>(InnoDB actually opens for connections after step 3 and runs step 4 in a=
 background thread; rows still being rolled back stay locked until it finis=
hes.)</p>
<p><strong>What recovery does with each kind of log entry:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Log Entry</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Transaction Status</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Recovery Action</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Change logged, T committed</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Committed</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>REDO</strong> =E2=80=94 replay the =
change</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Change logged, T not committed</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C Not committed</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>UNDO</strong> =E2=80=94 reverse the=
 change</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Change not logged</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=80=94</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">Nothing to do (change never happened)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p><strong>Where the files live:</strong> in MySQL =E2=89=A4 8.0.29 the red=
o log is <code>ib_logfile0</code> / <code>ib_logfile1</code> (sized by <cod=
e>innodb_log_file_size</code>); from 8.0.30 it lives in the <code>#innodb_r=
edo/</code> directory (sized by <code>innodb_redo_log_capacity</code>). In =
PostgreSQL it's the <code>pg_wal/</code> directory.</p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"mechanism-2-fsync--actually-getting-to-disk" data-toc=3D"Mechanis=
m 2: fsync() =E2=80=94 Actually Getting to Disk">Mechanism 2: <code>fsync()=
</code> =E2=80=94 Actually Getting to Disk</h3>
<p>Calling <code>write()</code> does <strong>not</strong> put your data on =
disk. It copies the bytes into a <strong>kernel buffer (the OS page cache)<=
/strong> and returns immediately. The data is still in <strong>volatile RAM=
</strong> and may sit there for seconds before reaching physical disk; a po=
wer cut during that window loses the &quot;written&quot; data.</p>
<p><code>fsync(fd)</code> is the system call that says <em>&quot;push every=
thing for this file all the way down to persistent media, and don't return =
until it's there.&quot;</em> InnoDB calls <code>fsync()</code> on the redo =
log at every commit.</p>
