strong>. At any given moment, you can inspect the database and ask: &quot;d=
oes every row obey every rule?&quot; If yes =E2=86=92 integrity holds.</p>
</div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"consistency--the-guarantee" data-toc=3D"Consistency =E2=80=94 The=
 Guarantee">Consistency =E2=80=94 The Guarantee</h3>
<p><strong>Consistency</strong> (the <strong>C</strong> in ACID) means a tr=
ansaction takes the database from <strong>one valid state to another valid =
state</strong>. It never leaves the database in a half-finished, rule-viola=
ting state.</p>
<h4 id=3D"example--bank-transfer-1">Example =E2=80=94 Bank Transfer</h4>
<p>The business rule (an integrity constraint): <strong>the total money in =
the system must never change during a transfer.</strong></p>
