</section><section class=3D"sec"><h2 id=3D"types-of-schedules-in-dbms" data=
-toc=3D"31. Types of Schedules in DBMS"><span class=3D"sec-n">31.</span> Ty=
pes of Schedules in DBMS</h2>
<p>=F0=9F=94=97 <strong>Reference:</strong> <a href=3D"https://www.geeksfor=
geeks.org/types-of-schedules-in-dbms/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener">G=
eeksforGeeks =E2=80=94 Types of Schedules in DBMS</a></p>
<p>A <strong>schedule</strong> is the chronological order in which operatio=
ns (read/write) of multiple concurrent transactions are executed. Choosing =
the right schedule ensures correctness and consistency.</p>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note"><p class=3D"markdown-aler=
t-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-info mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" ver=
