<h4 id=3D"testing-with-a-precedence-graph">Testing with a Precedence Graph<=
/h4>
<p>=F0=9F=94=97 <strong>References:</strong> <a href=3D"https://www.geeksfo=
rgeeks.org/dbms/conflict-serializability-in-dbms/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D=
"noopener">GeeksforGeeks =E2=80=94 Conflict Serializability in DBMS</a> =C2=
=B7 <a href=3D"https://www.javatpoint.com/dbms-conflict-serializable-schedu=
le" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener">Javatpoint =E2=80=94 Conflict Serial=
izable Schedule</a></p>
<p>To test if a schedule is conflict-serializable, build a <strong>preceden=
ce (dependency) graph</strong>:</p>
<ol>
<li>Create a node for each transaction</li>
<li>Draw an edge <code>Ti =E2=86=92 Tj</code> if Ti has a conflicting opera=
tion that appears <strong>before</strong> Tj's conflicting operation</li>
<li>If the graph has <strong>no cycle</strong> =E2=86=92 <strong>conflict s=
erializable</strong> =E2=9C=85</li>
<li>If the graph has a <strong>cycle</strong> =E2=86=92 <strong>NOT conflic=
t serializable</strong> =E2=9D=8C</li>
</ol>
