<hr>
<h3 id=3D"equivalence-schedules-summary" data-toc=3D"Equivalence Schedules =
Summary">Equivalence Schedules Summary</h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Type</th>
<th>Definition</th>
<th>How to Check</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Result Equivalent</strong></td>
<td>Produce same final result</td>
<td>Not reliable =E2=80=94 may vary with different data</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>View Equivalent</strong></td>
<td>Same initial reads, same read-from, same final writes</td>
<td>Check 3 conditions (complex)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Conflict Equivalent</strong></td>
<td>Same order of conflicting operations</td>
<td>Precedence graph (no cycle =3D =E2=9C=85)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"4-non-serializable-schedules" data-toc=3D"4. Non-Serializable Sch=
edules">4. Non-Serializable Schedules</h3>
<p>Schedules that are NOT equivalent to any serial schedule. They may or ma=
y not be safe depending on their <strong>recoverability</strong>.</p>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note"><p class=3D"markdown-aler=
t-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-info mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" ver=
sion=3D"1.1" width=3D"16" height=3D"16" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M0 =
8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13=
ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 =
0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1=
 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z"></path></svg>Note</p><p>Recoverability is a separate q=
uestion from serializability: the classes below (recoverable =E2=86=92 casc=
adeless =E2=86=92 strict) apply to any schedule. As the <a href=3D"#schedul=
e-hierarchy-venn-diagram">Schedule Hierarchy</a> shows, every serial schedu=
le is also strict.</p>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"4a-non-recoverable-schedule--must-avoid">4a. Non-Recoverable Sche=
dule =E2=9D=8C (Must AVOID)</h4>
<p>T2 reads T1's uncommitted data and <strong>commits before T1</strong>. I=
f T1 later aborts, T2 has committed with invalid data =E2=80=94 <strong>can=
not be undone</strong>.</p>
