</section><section class=3D"sec"><h2 id=3D"concurrency-problems-without-pro=
per-isolation" data-toc=3D"32. Concurrency Problems (Without Proper Isolati=
on)"><span class=3D"sec-n">32.</span> Concurrency Problems (Without Proper =
Isolation)</h2>
<p>=F0=9F=94=97 <strong>Reference:</strong> <a href=3D"https://www.geeksfor=
geeks.org/dbms/concurrency-problems-in-dbms-transactions/" target=3D"_blank=
" rel=3D"noopener">GeeksforGeeks =E2=80=94 Concurrency Problems in DBMS Tra=
nsactions</a></p>
<p>When multiple transactions run concurrently WITHOUT proper isolation, th=
ese problems can occur:</p>
<p><strong>The five problems, by conflict type</strong> (the naming used in=
 most textbooks and interviews):</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Problem</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Conflict type</th>
<th>What happens</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Dirty Read</strong> (temporary update)</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>W-R</strong></td>
<td>T2 reads data that T1 wrote but never committed</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Lost Update</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>W-W</strong></td>
<td>T1's write is silently overwritten by T2</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Incorrect Summary</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>R-W</strong></td>
<td>An aggregate (SUM, COUNT, AVG) mixes old and new values while another t=
ransaction updates the rows</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Non-Repeatable Read</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>R-W</strong></td>
<td>T1 reads the same row twice and gets different values</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Phantom Read</strong></td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>R-W</strong></td>
<td>T1 re-runs a query and gets a different <em>set</em> of rows because T2=
 inserted/deleted rows</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p><strong>Why we allow concurrency at all</strong> =E2=80=94 the trade-off=
 these problems buy us:</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Advantage</th>
<th>Why</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Reduced waiting time</strong></td>
<td>A short transaction isn't stuck behind a long one</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>High throughput</strong></td>
<td>More transactions complete per second</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>High resource utilization</strong></td>
<td>While one transaction waits on disk I/O, another uses the CPU</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note"><p class=3D"markdown-aler=
t-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-info mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" ver=
sion=3D"1.1" width=3D"16" height=3D"16" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M0 =
