<h4 id=3D"guarantees">Guarantees</h4>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note"><p class=3D"markdown-aler=
t-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-info mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" ver=
sion=3D"1.1" width=3D"16" height=3D"16" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M0 =
8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13=
ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 =
0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1=
 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z"></path></svg>Note</p><p><strong>2PL guarantees conflic=
t serializability</strong> =E2=80=94 if all transactions follow 2PL, the re=
sulting schedule is always equivalent to some serial schedule. =E2=9A=A0=EF=
=B8=8F Basic 2PL can still have <strong>cascading aborts</strong>, and =E2=
=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F <strong>deadlocks</strong> are possible.</p>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"variants-of-2pl">Variants of 2PL</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Variant</th>
<th>Rule</th>
<th>Prevents</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Basic 2PL</strong></td>
<td>Growing then shrinking</td>
<td>Conflict serializability</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Strict 2PL</strong></td>
<td>Hold ALL exclusive (X) locks until COMMIT/ABORT</td>
<td>Cascading rollbacks + serializability</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Rigorous 2PL</strong></td>
<td>Hold ALL locks (S and X) until COMMIT/ABORT</td>
<td>Cascading rollbacks + strictest serializability</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Conservative 2PL</strong> (Pre-Claiming)</td>
<td>Acquire <strong>ALL</strong> locks <strong>before</strong> the transact=
ion starts; if any is unavailable, acquire none and wait</td>
<td><strong>Deadlocks</strong> (no hold-and-wait) =E2=80=94 but poor concur=
rency</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note"><p class=3D"markdown-aler=
t-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-info mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 16" ver=
sion=3D"1.1" width=3D"16" height=3D"16" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M0 =
8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13=
ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 =
0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1=
 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z"></path></svg>Note</p><p><strong>Conservative 2PL is th=
e only deadlock-free variant</strong> =E2=80=94 it breaks the <em>hold and =
wait</em> condition by claiming every lock up front. The cost is that locks=
 are held for the entire transaction even if a row is only touched at the v=
ery end, and you must know all the locks in advance (often impossible). See=
 <a href=3D"#pre-claiming-lock-protocol">Pre-Claiming Lock Protocol</a> abo=
ve for how it works.</p>
</div>
