<h3 id=3D"3-timestamp-based-concurrency-control" data-toc=3D"3. Timestamp-B=
ased Concurrency Control">3. Timestamp-Based Concurrency Control</h3>
<p>Each transaction gets a <strong>unique timestamp</strong> when it starts=
. The DBMS ensures transactions execute in <strong>timestamp order</strong>=
 =E2=80=94 older transactions have priority.</p>
<h4 id=3D"the-three-timestamps-notation">The Three Timestamps (Notation)</h=
4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Short form</th>
<th>Full form</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>TS(Ti)</code></td>
<td><strong>Timestamp of transaction Ti</strong></td>
<td>When Ti <strong>started</strong>. Smaller =3D older transaction (higher=
 priority)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>W-TS(X)</code></td>
<td><strong>Write Timestamp of data item X</strong></td>
<td><code>TS</code> of the <strong>youngest transaction that has written</s=
trong> X so far</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>R-TS(X)</code></td>
<td><strong>Read Timestamp of data item X</strong></td>
<td><code>TS</code> of the <strong>youngest transaction that has read</stro=
ng> X so far</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>Each transaction carries one <code>TS</code>; each data item X carries i=
ts own <code>W-TS(X)</code> and <code>R-TS(X)</code>.</p>
