<hr>
<h4 id=3D"prevention-schemes-timestamp-based">Prevention Schemes (Timestamp=
-Based)</h4>
<p>Each transaction gets a <strong>timestamp</strong> at start =E2=80=94 a =
smaller timestamp means <strong>older</strong>. The scheme then decides who=
 waits and who dies.</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Scheme</th>
<th>Rule</th>
<th>Action</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Preemptive?</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>Wait-Die</strong></td>
<td>Older <strong>waits</strong>, younger <strong>dies</strong></td>
<td>If Ti is older than Tj =E2=86=92 Ti waits. If Ti is younger =E2=86=92 T=
i is rolled back (dies) and restarts with the <strong>same</strong> timesta=
mp</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9D=8C Non-preemptive</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>Wound-Wait</strong></td>
<td>Older <strong>wounds</strong>, younger <strong>waits</strong></td>
<td>If Ti is older than Tj =E2=86=92 Tj is rolled back (wounded). If Ti is =
younger =E2=86=92 Ti waits</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Preemptive</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=3D"text-align:center"><strong>Timeout-Based</strong></td>
<td>Wait only up to a limit</td>
<td>If the wait exceeds the threshold =E2=86=92 roll the waiter back. No ti=
mestamps or graph needed</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">=E2=9C=85 Preemptive</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
