InnoDB uses <strong>MVCC + 2PL</strong>. PostgreSQL uses <strong>MVCC + Ser=
ializable Snapshot Isolation (SSI)</strong>. Oracle uses <strong>MVCC</stro=
ng>. SQL Server uses <strong>Lock-based (2PL) with optional MVCC</strong> (=
snapshot isolation). Understanding that real databases combine multiple tec=
hniques is key.</p>
</div>
