</section><section class=3D"sec"><h2 id=3D"what-is-the-meaning-of-the-word-=
relational-in-rdbms" data-toc=3D"35. What Is the Meaning of the Word &quot;=
Relational&quot; =E2=80=A6"><span class=3D"sec-n">35.</span> What Is the Me=
aning of the Word &quot;Relational&quot; in RDBMS?</h2>
<p><strong>Common misconception =E2=9D=8C:</strong> &quot;Relational means =
tables are related to each other via foreign keys/joins.&quot; That's not w=
here the word comes from.</p>
<p><strong>Actual origin:</strong> It comes from <strong>E. F. Codd's 1970 =
paper</strong>, borrowing the mathematical term <strong>&quot;relation&quot=
;</strong> =E2=80=94 a set of <strong>tuples</strong> drawn from the Cartes=
ian product of <strong>domains</strong>. In plain English: a <strong>relati=
on</strong> is just a table, where each row is a tuple of values from fixed=
 columns.</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Mathematical Term</th>
<th>DBMS Equivalent</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Relation</strong></td>
<td>Table</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Tuple</strong></td>
<td>Row</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Attribute</strong></td>
<td>Column</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Domain</strong></td>
<td>Valid value set for a column</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>So &quot;the <code>employees</code> relation&quot; means the table itsel=
f =E2=80=94 not its relationships to other tables.</p>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-important"><p class=3D"markdown=
-alert-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-report mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 =
16" version=3D"1.1" width=3D"16" height=3D"16" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=
=3D"M0 1.75C0 .784.784 0 1.75 0h12.5C15.216 0 16 .784 16 1.75v9.5A1.75 1.75=
 0 0 1 14.25 13H8.06l-2.573 2.573A1.458 1.458 0 0 1 3 14.543V13H1.75A1.75 1=
.75 0 0 1 0 11.25Zm1.75-.25a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v9.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h2a.=
75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.19l2.72-2.72a.749.749 0 0 1 .53-.22h6.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .=
25-.25v-9.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25-.25Zm7 2.25v2.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.5 0v-2.5a.75.75=
 0 0 1 1.5 0ZM9 9a1 1 0 1 1-2 0 1 1 0 0 1 2 0Z"></path></svg>Important</p><=
p><strong>Why it matters:</strong> Because a relation is mathematically a <=
em>set</em>, it's the reason relational databases support <strong>Relationa=
