d Optimizer</h2>
<p>Before MySQL returns a single row, your SQL text goes through a fixed pi=
peline. Knowing the stages tells you <strong>where</strong> a problem lives=
: a syntax error dies in the parser, an &quot;unknown column&quot; dies in =
the preprocessor, and a slow-but-correct query is almost always an <strong>=
optimizer</strong> decision you disagree with.</p>
