<hr>
<h3 id=3D"stage-2--the-parser" data-toc=3D"Stage 2 =E2=80=94 The Parser">St=
age 2 =E2=80=94 The Parser</h3>
<p>The parser does two mechanical jobs and nothing else:</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Step</th>
<th>What Happens</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Lexical analysis</strong></td>
<td>Chops the SQL string into tokens: <code>SELECT</code>, <code>name</code=
>, <code>,</code>, <code>FROM</code>, <code>users</code>, <code>WHERE</code=
>, =E2=80=A6</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Syntax analysis</strong></td>
<td>Feeds tokens through MySQL's grammar to build a <strong>parse tree</str=
ong></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>The parser knows the <em>grammar</em> of SQL but nothing about <strong>y=
our</strong> database =E2=80=94 it has never heard of your tables.</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs">SELCT <span class=3D"hljs-operator">*</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyw=
ord">FROM</span> users;
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- =E2=9D=8C ERROR 1064 (42000): You have an e=
rror in your SQL syntax near &#x27;SELCT&#x27;</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">--    Caught by the PARSER =E2=80=94 &#x27;SEL=
CT&#x27; is not a valid token.</span></code></pre></div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"stage-3--the-preprocessor-the-precompiler-step" data-toc=3D"Stage=
 3 =E2=80=94 The Preprocessor (the &quot;precompiler&quot; step)">Stage 3 =
=E2=80=94 The Preprocessor (the &quot;precompiler&quot; step)</h3>
<p>The preprocessor takes the parse tree and checks it against <strong>real=
ity</strong>:</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Check</th>
<th>Example Failure</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Do the tables exist?</td>
<td><code>ERROR 1146: Table 'shop.userz' doesn't exist</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Do the columns exist?</td>
<td><code>ERROR 1054: Unknown column 'emial' in 'field list'</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Is a column name ambiguous?</td>
<td><code>ERROR 1052: Column 'id' in field list is ambiguous</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Does this user have privileges?</td>
<td><code>ERROR 1142: SELECT command denied to user...</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Expand views into their underlying query</td>
<td><code>SELECT * FROM v_active_users</code> =E2=86=92 the view's <code>SE=
LECT</code> is inlined</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> emial <span class=3D"hljs-=
keyword">FROM</span> users;
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- =E2=9C=85 Passes the PARSER  (syntactically=
 perfect)</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- =E2=9D=8C Dies in the PREPROCESSOR: Unknown=
 column &#x27;emial&#x27; in &#x27;field list&#x27;</span></code></pre></di=
v>
