<hr>
<hr>
</section><section class=3D"sec"><h2 id=3D"the-buffer-pool--how-data-actual=
ly-flows-between-disk-and-memory" data-toc=3D"38. The Buffer Pool =E2=80=94=
 How Data Actually Flows =E2=80=A6"><span class=3D"sec-n">38.</span> The Bu=
ffer Pool =E2=80=94 How Data Actually Flows Between Disk and Memory</h2>
<p>The <strong>buffer pool</strong> is the database's in-memory cache of <s=
trong>disk pages</strong>. It is the single most important performance stru=
cture in any DBMS, and the reason a query on a 500 GB table can return in a=
 millisecond.</p>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-important"><p class=3D"markdown=
-alert-title"><svg class=3D"octicon octicon-report mr-2" viewBox=3D"0 0 16 =
16" version=3D"1.1" width=3D"16" height=3D"16" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=
=3D"M0 1.75C0 .784.784 0 1.75 0h12.5C15.216 0 16 .784 16 1.75v9.5A1.75 1.75=
 0 0 1 14.25 13H8.06l-2.573 2.573A1.458 1.458 0 0 1 3 14.543V13H1.75A1.75 1=
.75 0 0 1 0 11.25Zm1.75-.25a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v9.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h2a.=
75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.19l2.72-2.72a.749.749 0 0 1 .53-.22h6.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .=
25-.25v-9.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25-.25Zm7 2.25v2.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.5 0v-2.5a.75.75=
 0 0 1 1.5 0ZM9 9a1 1 0 1 1-2 0 1 1 0 0 1 2 0Z"></path></svg>Important</p><=
p><strong>The one rule to remember:</strong> the database engine <strong>ne=
ver</strong> reads or writes a row directly on disk. It reads the <strong>p=
age</strong> containing that row into the buffer pool, works on the copy in=
 RAM, and writes the page back <strong>later</strong>.</p>
</div>
<p><strong>The unit is a page, not a row:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Engine</th>
<th style=3D"text-align:center">Page size</th>
<th>Buffer pool name</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>MySQL / InnoDB</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">16 KB</td>
<td>Buffer Pool (<code>innodb_buffer_pool_size</code>)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>PostgreSQL</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">8 KB</td>
<td>Shared Buffers (<code>shared_buffers</code>)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>SQL Server</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">8 KB</td>
<td>Buffer Cache</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Oracle</td>
<td style=3D"text-align:center">8 KB</td>
<td>Database Buffer Cache</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>Asking for one 200-byte row still loads the whole 16 KB page =E2=80=94 w=
hich is <em>good</em>, because the neighbouring rows are usually the ones y=
ou want next.</p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"key-terms--page-frame-dirty-clean-pinned" data-toc=3D"Key Terms =
=E2=80=94 Page, Frame, Dirty, Clean, Pinned">Key Terms =E2=80=94 Page, Fram=
e, Dirty, Clean, Pinned</h3>
<h4 id=3D"page-block">Page (block)</h4>
<p>A <strong>page</strong> is the <strong>fixed-size unit of I/O</strong> =
=E2=80=94 the smallest chunk the database will ever read from or write to d=
isk. Your table file is simply a long array of these pages, and a page hold=
s many rows plus some bookkeeping:</p>
