<h4 id=3D"frame">Frame</h4>
<p>A <strong>frame</strong> is one page-sized slot <strong>inside the buffe=
r pool</strong>. A buffer pool of 8 GB with 16 KB pages has ~524,000 frames=
. Each frame either sits empty or holds a copy of one disk page.</p>
<h4 id=3D"clean-vs-dirty--the-important-pair">Clean vs Dirty =E2=80=94 the =
important pair</h4>
<p>The distinction is simply: <strong>does the in-memory copy still match t=
he on-disk copy?</strong></p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th></th>
<th><strong>Clean page</strong></th>
<th><strong>Dirty page</strong></th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Definition</td>
<td>The RAM copy is <strong>identical</strong> to the disk copy</td>
<td>The RAM copy has been <strong>modified</strong>; disk still holds the o=
ld version</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Created by</td>
<td>Reading a page in, or flushing a dirty page</td>
<td>Any <code>INSERT</code> / <code>UPDATE</code> / <code>DELETE</code> tou=
ching that page</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Cost to evict</td>
<td><strong>Free</strong> =E2=80=94 just drop it, disk already has the trut=
h</td>
<td><strong>Expensive</strong> =E2=80=94 must be written to disk first</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Lost on crash?</td>
<td>Doesn't matter =E2=80=94 disk has the same bytes</td>
<td>=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F Yes =E2=80=94 recovered by <strong>replaying the WAL=
</strong></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<figure class=3D"diagram"><img class=3D"fig" src=3D"data:image/svg+xml;base=
64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSI3ODAiIGhl=
aWdodD0iMzY2IiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgNzgwIDM2NiIgZm9udC1mYW1pbHk9IlNlZ29lIFVJLCB=
JbnRlciwgc3lzdGVtLXVpLCAtYXBwbGUtc3lzdGVtLCBzYW5zLXNlcmlmIiBzdHlsZT0iZm9udC=
