<h4 id=3D"pinned-page">Pinned page</h4>
<p>While a query is actively reading or writing a page, the page is <strong=
>pinned</strong> (its pin/reference count is &gt; 0) so the eviction algori=
thm cannot steal it mid-operation. Once the operation finishes the page is =
unpinned and becomes a candidate for eviction again.</p>
<h4 id=3D"why-these-terms-matter">Why these terms matter</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Concept</th>
<th>Consequence</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Too many dirty pages</td>
<td>Eviction and checkpoints stall, because each victim must be written out=
 first =E2=80=94 writes start blocking</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Mostly clean pool</td>
<td>Evictions are instant, so a read-heavy workload stays fast</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Dirty pages at crash time</td>
<td>Exactly what WAL replay has to reconstruct =E2=80=94 more dirty pages m=
eans longer crash recovery</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Checkpoint</strong></td>
<td>The periodic operation that flushes dirty pages and records &quot;every=
thing before this point is safely on disk&quot;, so recovery doesn't have t=
o replay the whole log</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
