eks.org/need-for-dbms/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener">GeeksforGeeks =
=E2=80=94 Need for DBMS</a></p>
<p>This is the <strong>very first question</strong> in most DBMS interviews=
, and it's really asking: <em>&quot;do you understand what a database actua=
lly gives you that a folder of files does not?&quot;</em></p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"the-setup--how-the-pre-dbms-world-worked" data-toc=3D"The Setup =
=E2=80=94 How the Pre-DBMS World Worked">The Setup =E2=80=94 How the Pre-DB=
MS World Worked</h3>
<p>Before DBMSs, applications stored data in <strong>flat files</strong> (<=
code>.txt</code>, <code>.csv</code>, binary records) managed directly by th=
e operating system's file system. Every program had to open the file, parse=
 the bytes, find its record, and write it back itself.</p>
