te 500: a lost update" title=3D"Two concurrent =E2=82=B9500 withdrawals on =
plain files both read 1000 and write 500: a lost update" loading=3D"lazy"><=
/figure>
<p>A DBMS provides <strong>locks, MVCC, and isolation levels</strong> =E2=
=80=94 see <a href=3D"#concurrency-control-in-dbms-ski">Concurrency Control=
 in DBMS</a>.</p>
<h4 id=3D"7-security--access-control-problems">7. Security &amp; Access Con=
trol Problems</h4>
<p>File-system permissions are <strong>all-or-nothing per file</strong>. If=
 a clerk needs to read customer names, they get access to the whole file =
=E2=80=94 salaries, account numbers and all. There's no way to say &quot;th=
is user may read these <em>columns</em> of these <em>rows</em>&quot;.</p>
<p>A DBMS gives per-object, per-operation privileges plus <strong>views</st=
rong> to expose only a slice:</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">GRANT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword=
">SELECT</span> (name, city) <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ON</span> custome=
rs <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">TO</span> clerk_role;
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">VIE=
W</span> clerk_view <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">AS</span> <span class=3D"h=
ljs-keyword">SELECT</span> name, city <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FROM</sp=
an> customers <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> branch <span class=
=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;Pune&#x27;<=
/span>;</code></pre></div>
<p>See <a href=3D"#mysql-grant--revoke-privileges-detailed">GRANT / REVOKE =
Privileges</a> and <a href=3D"#sql-views">SQL Views</a>.</p>
<h4 id=3D"8-no-backup-recovery-or-crash-resilience">8. No Backup, Recovery,=
 or Crash Resilience</h4>
<p>If a file is corrupted or a disk dies mid-write, you restore last night'=
s copy and lose the day. A DBMS has <strong>WAL, redo/undo logs, checkpoint=
s, and point-in-time recovery</strong> =E2=80=94 see <a href=3D"#4-durabili=
ty--how-its-achieved">Durability =E2=80=94 How It's Achieved</a>.</p>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"file-system-vs-dbms--side-by-side-comparison" data-toc=3D"File Sy=
stem vs DBMS =E2=80=94 Side-by-Side Comparison">File System vs DBMS =E2=80=
=94 Side-by-Side Comparison</h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Aspect</th>
<th>File System</th>
<th>DBMS</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Data access</strong></td>
<td>Custom program per query</td>
<td>Declarative SQL + query optimizer</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Redundancy</strong></td>
<td>High =E2=80=94 same data in many files</td>
<td>Controlled via normalization &amp; foreign keys</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Consistency</strong></td>
<td>Manual; breaks easily</td>
<td>Enforced by constraints</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Integrity rules</strong></td>
<td>Coded in every application</td>
<td>Declared once in the schema</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Transactions (ACID)</strong></td>
<td>=E2=9D=8C None</td>
<td>=E2=9C=85 Atomicity, Consistency, Isolation, Durability</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Concurrency</strong></td>
<td>=E2=9D=8C No locking =E2=86=92 corruption</td>
<td>=E2=9C=85 Locks / MVCC / isolation levels</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Recovery after crash</strong></td>
<td>Restore from backup, lose recent work</td>
<td>Redo/undo logs, point-in-time recovery</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Security</strong></td>
<td>Per-file, all-or-nothing</td>
<td>Per-table / per-column / per-row, views, roles</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Relationships</strong></td>
<td>Hand-coded matching</td>
<td>Foreign keys + <code>JOIN</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Data independence</strong></td>
<td>=E2=9D=8C Change the format =E2=86=92 rewrite every program</td>
<td>=E2=9C=85 Physical &amp; logical independence via abstraction levels</t=
d>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Indexing / performance</strong></td>
<td>Manual, if at all</td>
<td>B-tree/hash indexes, statistics-driven optimizer</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Concurrent users</strong></td>
<td>Effectively one writer</td>
<td>Thousands</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Setup cost &amp; overhead</strong></td>
<td>=E2=9C=85 Almost none</td>
<td>=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F Server, schema design, tuning, licence</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Best for</strong></td>
<td>Config, logs, media blobs, one-off scripts</td>
<td>Shared, structured, concurrently-updated business data</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"when-a-file-system-is-still-the-right-choice" data-toc=3D"When a =
File System Is Still the Right Choice">When a File System Is Still the Righ=
t Choice</h3>
<p>An honest answer here scores well in interviews =E2=80=94 &quot;always u=
se a database&quot; is not true.</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Use a plain file when=E2=80=A6</th>
<th>Why</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Config / <code>.env</code> / YAML</td>
<td>Read once at startup; a DBMS is pure overhead</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Application logs</td>
<td>Append-only, write-heavy, rarely queried by key</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Images, video, PDFs (blobs)</td>
<td>Store the <strong>bytes</strong> on disk/S3, the <strong>metadata</stro=
ng> in the DBMS</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Data interchange (CSV export, batch feeds)</td>
<td>The file <em>is</em> the transport format</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>A single-user throwaway script</td>
<td>Nothing to coordinate, no concurrency</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
