</section><section class=3D"sec"><h2 id=3D"replication-in-mysql--read-repli=
cas-lag--failover" data-toc=3D"40. Replication in MySQL =E2=80=94 Read Repl=
icas, Lag &amp; =E2=80=A6"><span class=3D"sec-n">40.</span> Replication in =
MySQL =E2=80=94 Read Replicas, Lag &amp; Failover</h2>
<p>=F0=9F=94=97 <strong>Reference:</strong> <a href=3D"https://dev.mysql.co=
m/doc/refman/8.0/en/replication.html" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener">My=
SQL Docs =E2=80=94 Replication</a> =C2=B7 <a href=3D"https://dev.mysql.com/=
doc/refman/8.0/en/replication-semisync.html" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noope=
ner">Semisynchronous Replication</a></p>
<p><strong>Replication</strong> =3D keeping copies of the same data on seve=
ral MySQL servers. One server, the <strong>source</strong> (primary), takes=
 the writes; the <strong>replicas</strong> copy every change. (MySQL 8.0.22=
+ says <em>source/replica</em>; older docs say <em>master/slave</em>.)</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Why replicate?</th>
<th>How replicas help</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>High availability</strong></td>
<td>If the source dies, promote a replica (<strong>failover</strong>)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Read scaling</strong></td>
<td>Send <code>SELECT</code>s to replicas; the source handles only writes</=
td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Durability</strong></td>
<td>Data survives the loss of a whole machine (<a href=3D"#mechanism-5-repl=
ication--cross-machine-durability">Mechanism 5</a>)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Offloading</strong></td>
<td>Run backups, reports and analytics on a replica, not on the source</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Geography</strong></td>
<td>Put a replica near users in another region for fast local reads</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<div class=3D"markdown-alert markdown-alert-warning"><p class=3D"markdown-a=
