aXRlLjwvdGV4dD4KPC9zdmc+Cg=3D=3D" alt=3D"MySQL replication: the app sends w=
rites to the source, which records each commit in its binary log; each repl=
ica's receiver (I/O) thread pulls binlog events into its relay log, and app=
lier (SQL) threads replay them; reads go to replicas through a proxy" title=
=3D"MySQL replication: the app sends writes to the source, which records ea=
ch commit in its binary log; each replica's receiver (I/O) thread pulls bin=
log events into its relay log, and applier (SQL) threads replay them; reads=
 go to replicas through a proxy" loading=3D"lazy"></figure>
<ol>
<li><strong>Source writes the binary log (binlog).</strong> Every committed=
 transaction is appended to the source's binlog as events.</li>
<li><strong>Replica's receiver thread</strong> (the &quot;I/O thread&quot;)=
 connects to the source, pulls new binlog events and writes them to a local=
 <strong>relay log</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>Replica's applier threads</strong> (the &quot;SQL threads&quot;=
) read the relay log and <strong>replay</strong> the changes on the replica=
's own tables. MySQL 8.0.27+ uses <strong>4 parallel applier workers</stron=
g> by default (<code>replica_parallel_workers</code>) and keeps the source'=
s commit order.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Binlog formats</strong> =E2=80=94 what gets shipped:</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Format</th>
<th>Ships</th>
<th>Trade-off</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>ROW</code> (<strong>default</strong> since 5.7.7)</td>
<td>The <strong>changed rows</strong> (before/after images)</td>
<td>Exact and safe. Big for mass updates (<code>UPDATE</code> of 1M rows =
=3D 1M row events)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>STATEMENT</code></td>
<td>The <strong>SQL text</strong></td>
<td>Small, but unsafe for non-deterministic SQL (<code>NOW()</code>, <code>=
UUID()</code>, <code>LIMIT</code> without <code>ORDER BY</code>)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>MIXED</code></td>
<td>Statement, switching to row when unsafe</td>
<td>Compromise; rarely chosen today</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<h4 id=3D"gtid--global-transaction-identifier">GTID =E2=80=94 Global Transa=
ction Identifier</h4>
<p>A <strong>GTID</strong> is a unique ID that MySQL gives to <strong>every=
 committed transaction</strong>. It's assigned on the source and <strong>st=
ays the same on every replica</strong>.</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">text</span></div><pre><code class=3D=
"hljs">3e11fa47-71ca-11e1-9e33-c80aa9429562:23
=E2=94=94=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=
=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80 server_uuid =E2=94=80=E2=94=80=
=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=
=94=80=E2=94=98 =E2=94=94=E2=94=98 23rd transaction committed on that serve=
r</code></pre></div>
<p>Each server records what it has applied as a compact set of ranges: <cod=
e>SELECT @@GLOBAL.gtid_executed;</code> =E2=86=92 <code>3e11fa47-=E2=80=A6:=
1-1000</code>.</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th></th>
<th><strong>Without GTID</strong> (binlog file + position)</th>
<th><strong>With GTID</strong></th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Replica's progress</td>
<td><code>mysql-bin.000042 : 8571</code>, only valid on <strong>one</strong=
> server</td>
<td><code>uuid:1-1000</code>, valid on <strong>every</strong> server</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Re-pointing after failover</td>
<td>Work out the matching file and offset on the new source by hand</td>
<td><code>CHANGE REPLICATION SOURCE TO =E2=80=A6 SOURCE_AUTO_POSITION =3D 1=
</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Same transaction applied twice?</td>
<td>Possible if the position is wrong</td>
<td><strong>Never</strong>: a server skips any GTID it already has</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p><strong>Used for:</strong> picking the most up-to-date replica at <a hre=
f=3D"#failover--when-the-source-dies">failover</a>, <a href=3D"#the-read-yo=
ur-own-writes-problem">read-your-own-writes</a> (<code>WAIT_FOR_EXECUTED_GT=
ID_SET</code>), and spotting <strong>errant transactions</strong> (a GTID c=
arrying a replica's own UUID means someone wrote to that replica).</p>
<p><strong>Enable:</strong> <code>gtid_mode =3D ON</code> and <code>enforce=
_gtid_consistency =3D ON</code> in <code>my.cnf</code>.</p>
<hr>
