<h3 id=3D"proxysql--the-mysql-aware-proxy" data-toc=3D"ProxySQL =E2=80=94 T=
he MySQL-Aware Proxy">ProxySQL =E2=80=94 The MySQL-Aware Proxy</h3>
<p><strong>ProxySQL</strong> is an open-source proxy that sits <strong>betw=
een your application and your MySQL servers</strong>. It speaks the MySQL p=
rotocol, so the app connects to ProxySQL (default port <strong>6033</strong=
>) exactly as if it were a MySQL server. ProxySQL then decides <strong>whic=
h real server</strong> each query goes to.</p>
<p>Unlike a plain TCP load balancer, it <strong>understands SQL</strong>: i=
