<h4 id=3D"what-it-does">What It Does</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Feature</th>
<th>What it means</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Hostgroups</strong></td>
<td>Servers are grouped, e.g. <strong>hostgroup 10 =3D writer</strong> (the=
 source), <strong>hostgroup 20 =3D readers</strong> (replicas). Queries are=
 routed to a hostgroup, not to a single server</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Query rules (read/write split)</strong></td>
<td>Regex rules on each query: <code>SELECT =E2=80=A6 FOR UPDATE</code> =E2=
=86=92 writer, other <code>SELECT</code> =E2=86=92 readers, everything else=
 =E2=86=92 writer. <strong>No application code change</strong></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Connection pooling &amp; multiplexing</strong></td>
<td>Thousands of app connections share a small pool of backend connections,=
 which protects MySQL from connection storms</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Health &amp; lag checks</strong></td>
<td>Pings every server; a replica lagging more than <code>max_replication_l=
ag</code> seconds is temporarily <strong>shunned</strong> (no reads sent to=
 it)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Failover awareness</strong></td>
<td>Watches each server's <code>read_only</code> flag. When a replica is pr=
omoted (read_only =E2=86=92 OFF), ProxySQL <strong>automatically moves it i=
nto the writer hostgroup</strong>, so the app follows the new source with n=
o config change</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Query control</strong></td>
<td>Cache results of chosen queries, rewrite queries, block dangerous ones =
(firewall)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Observability</strong></td>
<td>Per-query-pattern stats (count, total/avg time) in <code>stats_mysql_qu=
ery_digest</code>: a free &quot;top slow queries&quot; view</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p><strong>Configuration</strong> is done through an SQL-like admin interfa=
ce (port 6032) and applied live, without a restart:</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- servers: source in writer hostgroup 1=
0, replicas in reader hostgroup 20</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INSERT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INT=
O</span> mysql_servers (hostgroup_id, hostname, port, max_replication_lag) =
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">VALUES</span>
  (<span class=3D"hljs-number">10</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27=
;db-source&#x27;</span>,  <span class=3D"hljs-number">3306</span>, <span cl=
ass=3D"hljs-number">0</span>),
  (<span class=3D"hljs-number">20</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27=
;db-replica1&#x27;</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">3306</span>, <span c=
lass=3D"hljs-number">5</span>),     <span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- shun th=
is replica if it lags &gt; 5 s</span>
  (<span class=3D"hljs-number">20</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27=
;db-replica2&#x27;</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">3306</span>, <span c=
lass=3D"hljs-number">5</span>);

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- let ProxySQL move servers between 10 and 20=
 based on their read_only flag</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INSERT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INT=
O</span> mysql_replication_hostgroups (writer_hostgroup, reader_hostgroup) =
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">VALUES</span> (<span class=3D"hljs-number">10<=
/span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">20</span>);

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- read/write split rules (checked in rule_id =
order)</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INSERT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">INT=
O</span> mysql_query_rules (rule_id, active, match_digest, destination_host=
group, apply) <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">VALUES</span>
  (<span class=3D"hljs-number">1</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">1</spa=
n>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;^SELECT.*FOR UPDATE&#x27;</span>, <sp=
an class=3D"hljs-number">10</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">1</span>), =
  <span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- locking reads =E2=86=92 writer</span>
  (<span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">1</spa=
n>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;^SELECT&#x27;</span>,             <sp=
an class=3D"hljs-number">20</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">1</span>); =
  <span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- other reads   =E2=86=92 readers</span>
