E MYSQL SERVERS <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">TO</span> DISK;
LOAD MYSQL QUERY RULES <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">TO</span> RUNTIME;  SAV=
E MYSQL QUERY RULES <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">TO</span> DISK;</code></pr=
e></div>
<h4 id=3D"benefits-vs-drawbacks">Benefits vs Drawbacks</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>=E2=9C=85 Benefits</th>
<th>=E2=9D=8C Drawbacks</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Read/write split <strong>without changing app code</strong></td>
<td><strong>One more hop</strong> (small extra latency) and one more compon=
ent to run and monitor</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Connection multiplexing</strong>: fewer MySQL connections, less=
 memory and CPU on the database</td>
<td>It can become a <strong>single point of failure</strong>: run 2+ ProxyS=
QL nodes (ProxySQL Cluster), or one on each app server</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Lag-aware</strong>: stops reading from replicas that fall behin=
d</td>
<td>Regex rules can route wrongly, e.g. a <code>SELECT</code> inside a tran=
saction that must see its own writes. Rules need care and testing</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Follows failover automatically</strong> via the <code>read_only=
</code> flag</td>
<td><strong>Doesn't do the promotion itself</strong>: it only re-routes. Yo=
u still need Orchestrator, MHA or Group Replication to promote a replica</t=
d>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Query caching, rewriting, firewall, per-query stats</td>
<td>Multiplexing is switched off for some sessions (open transactions, temp=
 tables, session variables, <code>LAST_INSERT_ID()</code>)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Changes apply live through the admin interface</td>
<td>Read-your-own-writes is still your problem unless you enable GTID causa=
l reads</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<h4 id=3D"protecting-mysql-from-connection-storms">Protecting MySQL from Co=
nnection Storms</h4>
<p><strong>Scenario:</strong> a buggy or misconfigured client opens <strong=
>1,000 connections</strong>. Without a proxy, MySQL creates 1,000 threads, =
or starts rejecting everyone with &quot;Too many connections&quot; once it =
hits <code>max_connections</code>. With ProxySQL in front, those 1,000 conn=
ections land on <strong>ProxySQL</strong>, and MySQL only ever sees a small=
, capped pool.</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Layer</th>
<th>Setting</th>
<th>Protection</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Per MySQL server</strong></td>
<td><code>mysql_servers.max_connections</code> (default 1000)</td>
<td>Hard cap on connections ProxySQL opens <strong>to each server</strong>.=
 MySQL can never get more, however many clients connect. <strong>This is th=
e key protection</strong></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Per user</strong></td>
<td><code>mysql_users.max_connections</code> (default 10000)</td>
<td>Caps client connections for <strong>one user</strong>. The noisy app hi=
ts its own limit and gets errors; other apps keep working</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Global</strong></td>
<td><code>mysql-max_connections</code> (default 2048)</td>
<td>Total client connections ProxySQL itself accepts</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Queue, don't fail</strong></td>
<td><code>mysql-connect_timeout_server_max</code> (default 10 s)</td>
<td>When a server's pool is full, the query <strong>waits</strong> for a fr=
ee connection and errors only after the timeout</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Throttle / block</strong></td>
<td>Query rules: <code>delay</code>, <code>timeout</code>, <code>error_msg<=
/code></td>
<td>Slow down, time out or reject a specific user's or query's traffic</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">UPDATE</span> mysql_servers <span class=
=3D"hljs-keyword">SET</span> max_connections <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=
=3D</span> <span class=3D"hljs-number">100</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keywo=
rd">WHERE</span> hostname <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span cl=
ass=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;db-source&#x27;</span>;   <span class=3D"hljs-com=
ment">-- MySQL sees at most 100</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">UPDATE</span> mysql_users   <span class=3D"hlj=
s-keyword">SET</span> max_connections <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</sp=
an> <span class=3D"hljs-number">200</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHE=
RE</span> username <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <span class=3D"=
hljs-string">&#x27;report_app&#x27;</span>;  <span class=3D"hljs-comment">-=
- noisy app capped at 200</span>
LOAD MYSQL SERVERS <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">TO</span> RUNTIME;  LOAD MY=
SQL USERS <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">TO</span> RUNTIME;
SAVE MYSQL SERVERS <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">TO</span> DISK;     SAVE MY=
SQL USERS <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">TO</span> DISK;</code></pre></div>
