ong> &quot;HAProxy balances <strong>connections</strong>; ProxySQL routes <=
strong>queries</strong>. For a MySQL source with replicas I'd use ProxySQL =
for automatic read/write splitting, connection pooling and lag-aware routin=
g. HAProxy is great when I only need fast TCP load balancing and the app al=
ready knows where to send writes. MySQL Router is the third option, the off=
icial choice with InnoDB Cluster.&quot;</p>
