<hr>
<h3 id=3D"replication-lag" data-toc=3D"Replication Lag">Replication Lag</h3=
>
<p><strong>Lag</strong> =3D how far a replica's applied state is behind the=
 source. Even &quot;fast&quot; async replication is usually milliseconds to=
 seconds behind, and under load it can be minutes.</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Common cause</th>
<th>Why it lags</th>
<th>Fix</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>One huge transaction</strong> (<code>DELETE</code> of 10M rows)=
</td>
<td>Replays on the replica for as long as it ran on the source, and transac=
tions queued behind it wait</td>
<td>Batch large writes (<code>=E2=80=A6 LIMIT 10000</code> in a loop)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Big <code>ALTER TABLE</code></strong></td>
<td>Replays on the replica after it finished on the source</td>
<td>Online schema tools (<a href=3D"#production-tools-for-zero-downtime-alt=
er">gh-ost / pt-osc</a>)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Too little apply parallelism</strong></td>
<td>One applier can't keep up with many concurrent writers on the source</t=
d>
<td>Raise <code>replica_parallel_workers</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Weak replica / heavy queries on it</strong></td>
<td>Reports compete with the applier for CPU and I/O</td>
<td>Same-size hardware; separate reporting replica</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Network</strong> (cross-region)</td>
<td>Events take longer to arrive</td>
<td>Expect it; design reads around it</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p><strong>Measuring it:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SHOW</span> REPLICA STATUS\G
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">--  Replica_IO_Running: Yes      =E2=86=90 rec=
eiver thread alive?</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">--  Replica_SQL_Running: Yes     =E2=86=90 app=
lier alive?</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">--  Seconds_Behind_Source: 3     =E2=86=90 rou=
gh lag (NULL =3D applier not running!)</span></code></pre></div>
<p><code>Seconds_Behind_Source</code> is approximate: it compares event tim=
estamps and can read 0 while the receiver itself is behind. For accurate nu=
mbers, write a heartbeat row on the source every second and compare it on t=
he replica (<code>pt-heartbeat</code>), or compare GTID sets.</p>
<hr>
