<h4 id=3D"when-to-use-vertical-partitioning">When to Use Vertical Partition=
ing</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>=E2=9C=85 Use When</th>
<th>=E2=9D=8C Avoid When</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Some columns are read much more frequently than others</td>
<td>All columns are always accessed together</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Table has large <code>TEXT</code>, <code>BLOB</code>, or <code>JSON</co=
de> columns mixed with small columns</td>
<td>Table is already narrow (few, small columns)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>You want to fit hot data entirely in the buffer pool</td>
<td>The overhead of <code>JOIN</code>ing tables back is unacceptable (ultra=
-low-latency systems)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Different columns have different security/access requirements</td>
<td>Table is small enough that row size doesn't matter</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"horizontal-partitioning" data-toc=3D"Horizontal Partitioning">Hor=
izontal Partitioning</h3>
<p>Horizontal partitioning means <strong>splitting a table's rows</strong> =
into multiple smaller tables (or partitions). Each partition has the <stron=
g>same columns</strong> but holds only a <strong>subset of the rows</strong=
>. The split is done based on a <strong>partition key</strong> =E2=80=94 a =
column (or expression) whose value determines which partition a row goes in=
to.</p>
<h4 id=3D"why-do-it-1">Why Do It?</h4>
<p>When a table grows to hundreds of millions of rows:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Index size exceeds memory</strong> =E2=80=94 the B+ Tree doesn'=
t fit in the buffer pool, causing frequent disk reads even for indexed quer=
ies</li>
<li><strong>Range scans read too many pages</strong> =E2=80=94 scanning a m=
onth of orders out of 5 years touches only 1.6% of the data, but without pa=
rtitioning the index covers all 5 years</li>
<li><strong>Maintenance operations are slow</strong> =E2=80=94 <code>ALTER =
TABLE</code>, <code>OPTIMIZE TABLE</code>, archiving old data take forever =
on a massive table</li>
<li><strong>Deleting old data is expensive</strong> =E2=80=94 <code>DELETE =
FROM orders WHERE order_date &lt; '2020-01-01'</code> generates billions of=
 undo log entries; dropping a partition is instant</li>
</ul>
<h4 id=3D"types-of-horizontal-partitioning">Types of Horizontal Partitionin=
g</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Type</th>
<th>How Rows Are Split</th>
<th>Best For</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Range</strong></td>
<td>By a continuous range of values (<code>date</code>, <code>id</code>)</t=
d>
<td>Time-series data, logs, orders</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>List</strong></td>
<td>By exact values from a defined list (<code>country</code>, <code>status=
</code>)</td>
<td>Region-based or category-based splits</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Hash</strong></td>
<td>By hash of a column value (evenly distributes rows)</td>
<td>Uniform distribution when there's no natural range</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Key</strong></td>
<td>Like hash but uses MySQL's internal hashing function</td>
<td>Simple even distribution</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<h4 id=3D"example--e-commerce-orders-table-range-partitioning-by-date">Exam=
ple =E2=80=94 E-Commerce Orders Table (Range Partitioning by Date)</h4>
<p>Suppose you have an <code>orders</code> table with 500 million rows span=
ning 5 years:</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- BEFORE: One massive table</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">TAB=
LE</span> orders (
    id           <span class=3D"hljs-type">BIGINT</span> <span class=3D"hlj=
s-keyword">PRIMARY</span> KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,
    customer_id  <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span>,
    order_date   <span class=3D"hljs-type">DATE</span>,
    total        <span class=3D"hljs-type">DECIMAL</span>(<span class=3D"hl=
js-number">10</span>,<span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>),
    status       ENUM(<span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;pending&#x27;</span=
>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;shipped&#x27;</span>, <span class=3D"h=
ljs-string">&#x27;delivered&#x27;</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27=
;cancelled&#x27;</span>)
);
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- 500 million rows, indexes are 40+ GB, queri=
es are getting slow</span></code></pre></div>
<h4 id=3D"after-horizontal-partitioning-range-by-year">After Horizontal Par=
titioning (Range by Year)</h4>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keywor=
d">TABLE</span> orders (
    id           <span class=3D"hljs-type">BIGINT</span> AUTO_INCREMENT,
    customer_id  <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span>,
    order_date   <span class=3D"hljs-type">DATE</span>,
    total        <span class=3D"hljs-type">DECIMAL</span>(<span class=3D"hl=
js-number">10</span>,<span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>),
    status       ENUM(<span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;pending&#x27;</span=
>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;shipped&#x27;</span>, <span class=3D"h=
ljs-string">&#x27;delivered&#x27;</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27=
;cancelled&#x27;</span>),
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PRIMARY</span> KEY (id, order_date)    <sp=
an class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Partition key MUST be part of the primary key<=
/span>
) <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PARTITION</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword=
">BY</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">RANGE</span> (<span class=3D"hljs-=
keyword">YEAR</span>(order_date)) (
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PARTITION</span> p2021 <span class=3D"hljs=
-keyword">VALUES</span> LESS THAN (<span class=3D"hljs-number">2022</span>)=
,
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PARTITION</span> p2022 <span class=3D"hljs=
-keyword">VALUES</span> LESS THAN (<span class=3D"hljs-number">2023</span>)=
,
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PARTITION</span> p2023 <span class=3D"hljs=
-keyword">VALUES</span> LESS THAN (<span class=3D"hljs-number">2024</span>)=
,
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PARTITION</span> p2024 <span class=3D"hljs=
-keyword">VALUES</span> LESS THAN (<span class=3D"hljs-number">2025</span>)=
,
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PARTITION</span> p2025 <span class=3D"hljs=
-keyword">VALUES</span> LESS THAN (<span class=3D"hljs-number">2026</span>)=
,
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PARTITION</span> p_future <span class=3D"h=
ljs-keyword">VALUES</span> LESS THAN MAXVALUE
);</code></pre></div>
