<h4 id=3D"partition-pruning--the-magic-that-makes-it-fast">Partition Prunin=
g =E2=80=94 The Magic That Makes It Fast</h4>
<p>When your query's <code>WHERE</code> clause includes the partition key, =
MySQL's optimizer automatically skips partitions that can't contain matchin=
g rows. This is called <strong>partition pruning</strong>.</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Find all orders in January 2025</span=
>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-operator">*<=
/span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FROM</span> orders
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> order_date <span class=3D"hljs-ke=
yword">BETWEEN</span> <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;2025-01-01&#x27;</s=
pan> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">AND</span> <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#=
x27;2025-01-31&#x27;</span>;

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- MySQL ONLY scans partition p2025 (~120M row=
s)</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- It completely SKIPS p2021, p2022, p2023, p2=
024 (380M rows ignored!)</span>

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- You can verify with EXPLAIN:</span>
EXPLAIN <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-oper=
ator">*</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FROM</span> orders <span class=
=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> order_date <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">BETW=
EEN</span> <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;2025-01-01&#x27;</span> <span =
class=3D"hljs-keyword">AND</span> <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;2025-01=
-31&#x27;</span>;
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Shows: partitions =3D p2025   =E2=86=90 onl=
y one partition scanned</span></code></pre></div>
<p><strong>Without partitioning:</strong> MySQL scans the index across all =
500M rows.
<strong>With partitioning:</strong> MySQL scans only the ~120M rows in the =
relevant partition =E2=80=94 <strong>4=C3=97 less data</strong>.</p>
<h4 id=3D"other-partitioning-types--examples">Other Partitioning Types =E2=
=80=94 Examples</h4>
<p><strong>List Partitioning (by country/region):</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keywor=
d">TABLE</span> customers (
    id         <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span> AUTO_INCREMENT,
    name       <span class=3D"hljs-type">VARCHAR</span>(<span class=3D"hljs=
-number">100</span>),
    country    <span class=3D"hljs-type">VARCHAR</span>(<span class=3D"hljs=
-number">2</span>),
    email      <span class=3D"hljs-type">VARCHAR</span>(<span class=3D"hljs=
-number">255</span>),
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PRIMARY</span> KEY (id, country)
) <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PARTITION</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword=
">BY</span> LIST COLUMNS (country) (
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PARTITION</span> p_india   <span class=3D"=
hljs-keyword">VALUES</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">IN</span> (<span c=
lass=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;IN&#x27;</span>),
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PARTITION</span> p_usa     <span class=3D"=
hljs-keyword">VALUES</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">IN</span> (<span c=
lass=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;US&#x27;</span>),
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PARTITION</span> p_europe  <span class=3D"=
hljs-keyword">VALUES</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">IN</span> (<span c=
lass=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;GB&#x27;</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x=
27;DE&#x27;</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;FR&#x27;</span>, <spa=
n class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;IT&#x27;</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">=
&#x27;ES&#x27;</span>),
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PARTITION</span> p_others  <span class=3D"=
hljs-keyword">VALUES</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">IN</span> (<span c=
lass=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;JP&#x27;</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x=
27;BR&#x27;</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;AU&#x27;</span>, <spa=
n class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;CA&#x27;</span>)
);

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Query: all Indian customers =E2=80=94 scans=
 ONLY p_india</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> <span class=3D"hljs-operator">*<=
/span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FROM</span> customers <span class=3D"hl=
js-keyword">WHERE</span> country <span class=3D"hljs-operator">=3D</span> <=
span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;IN&#x27;</span>;</code></pre></div>
<p><strong>Hash Partitioning (even distribution):</strong></p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">CREATE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keywor=
d">TABLE</span> sessions (
    id         <span class=3D"hljs-type">BIGINT</span> AUTO_INCREMENT,
    user_id    <span class=3D"hljs-type">INT</span>,
    data       JSON,
    created_at DATETIME,
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PRIMARY</span> KEY (id, user_id)
) <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">PARTITION</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword=
">BY</span> HASH(user_id)
  PARTITIONS <span class=3D"hljs-number">8</span>;

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- MySQL distributes rows across 8 partitions =
using: user_id MOD 8</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Each partition holds ~12.5% of the data</sp=
an>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Queries with WHERE user_id =3D ? only scan =
1 of 8 partitions</span></code></pre></div>
<h4 id=3D"dropping-old-data--the-killer-feature">Dropping Old Data =E2=80=
=94 The Killer Feature</h4>
<p>Without partitioning, deleting old data is brutal:</p>
<div class=3D"code"><div class=3D"code-bar"><span class=3D"dots"><i></i><i>=
</i><i></i></span><span class=3D"lang">SQL</span></div><pre><code class=3D"=
hljs"><span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- WITHOUT partitioning: generates massi=
ve undo logs, locks rows, takes hours</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">DELETE</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">FRO=
M</span> orders <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> order_date <span =
class=3D"hljs-operator">&lt;</span> <span class=3D"hljs-string">&#x27;2022-=
01-01&#x27;</span>;
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- Deletes 80 million rows one by one =F0=9F=
=94=A5</span>

<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- WITH partitioning: instant, zero overhead</=
span>
<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ALTER</span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">TABL=
E</span> orders <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">DROP</span> <span class=3D"hlj=
s-keyword">PARTITION</span> p2021;
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">-- 80 million rows gone in milliseconds =E2=80=
=94 it just deletes the partition&#x27;s data file</span></code></pre></div=
>
<h4 id=3D"when-to-use-horizontal-partitioning">When to Use Horizontal Parti=
tioning</h4>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>=E2=9C=85 Use When</th>
<th>=E2=9D=8C Avoid When</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Table has hundreds of millions or billions of rows</td>
<td>Table has &lt; 10 million rows (indexes handle it fine)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Queries almost always filter on the partition key (e.g., date range)</t=
d>
<td>Queries rarely include the partition key in <code>WHERE</code> (no prun=
ing =3D no benefit)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>You need to efficiently archive/delete old data</td>
<td>You need strong foreign key constraints (partitioned tables don't suppo=
rt FK in MySQL)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Time-series data: logs, events, orders, transactions</td>
<td>You need many unique indexes across all rows (unique constraints must i=
nclude the partition key)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Each partition can be maintained independently</td>
<td>The table is already fast enough with proper indexing</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"vertical-vs-horizontal-partitioning--comparison" data-toc=3D"Vert=
ical vs Horizontal Partitioning =E2=80=94 Comparison">Vertical vs Horizonta=
l Partitioning =E2=80=94 Comparison</h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Aspect</th>
<th>Vertical Partitioning</th>
<th>Horizontal Partitioning</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>What is split</strong></td>
<td>Columns</td>
<td>Rows</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Number of rows per partition</strong></td>
<td>Same (all rows exist in each sub-table)</td>
<td>Different (rows are distributed)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Number of columns per partition</strong></td>
<td>Fewer (each sub-table has a subset of columns)</td>
<td>Same (every partition has all columns)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Primary use case</strong></td>
<td>Separate hot (frequently accessed) columns from cold (rarely accessed) =
columns</td>
<td>Split a massive table into smaller chunks by a key</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>How to recombine</strong></td>
<td><code>JOIN</code> the sub-tables on the shared primary key</td>
<td><code>UNION ALL</code> across partitions (MySQL does this automatically=
)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Implementation</strong></td>
<td>Manual =E2=80=94 create separate tables and manage the split in your ap=
plication/queries</td>
<td>Built-in =E2=80=94 <code>CREATE TABLE ... PARTITION BY</code> (MySQL ha=
ndles it transparently)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>When it shines</strong></td>
<td>Wide tables with mixed access patterns (hot + cold columns)</td>
<td>Very large tables where queries always filter on the partition key</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Real-world example</strong></td>
<td>Splitting a <code>users</code> table into <code>users_core</code> (name=
, email) + <code>users_profile</code> (bio, avatar)</td>
<td>Splitting an <code>orders</code> table by year so each year is a separa=
te partition</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
