p><strong>Key takeaway:</strong> Vertical partitioning solves the <strong>&=
quot;too many columns&quot;</strong> problem (wide rows waste memory). Hori=
zontal partitioning solves the <strong>&quot;too many rows&quot;</strong> p=
roblem (massive tables overwhelm indexes and I/O). Use them based on your b=
ottleneck =E2=80=94 or combine both when the table is both wide and tall.</=
p>
