<hr>
<h3 id=3D"partition-based-data-retention-ttl-rotation" data-toc=3D"Partitio=
n-Based Data Retention (TTL Rotation)">Partition-Based Data Retention (TTL =
Rotation)</h3>
<p>When your team drops partitions older than 7 days to delete old data, th=
is process is called <strong>Partition-Based Data Retention</strong> or <st=
rong>TTL (Time-To-Live) Rotation</strong>. It's a widely used pattern in pr=
oduction systems for managing time-series data like logs, events, metrics, =
sessions, and transactional records that don't need to be kept forever.</p>
<h4 id=3D"what-is-it">What Is It?</h4>
<p>Instead of running expensive <code>DELETE</code> queries to remove old r=
ows, you:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Partition the table by date</strong> (one partition per day, we=
ek, or month)</li>
<li><strong>Drop entire partitions</strong> when they exceed the retention =
period (e.g., 7 days)</li>
<li><strong>Add new partitions</strong> ahead of time so incoming data alwa=
ys has a place to land</li>
</ol>
