p><strong>Rule of thumb:</strong> sharding is the <strong>last</strong> ste=
p, not the first. Try, in order: fixing queries and indexes, a bigger serve=
r, read replicas and caching, then partitioning and archiving old data. Sha=
rd only when <strong>writes or total data</strong> outgrow one primary.</p>
