<hr>
<h3 id=3D"memory--buffer-pool" data-toc=3D"Memory &amp; Buffer Pool">Memory=
 &amp; Buffer Pool</h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Flag</th>
<th>Default</th>
<th>What it controls</th>
<th>When to change</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_buffer_pool_size</code></td>
<td>128 MB</td>
<td>Size of the <a href=3D"#the-buffer-pool--how-data-actually-flows-betwee=
n-disk-and-memory">buffer pool</a>, the RAM cache of data and index pages. =
<strong>The single most important flag</strong></td>
<td>Dedicated DB server: <strong>50=E2=80=9375% of RAM</strong>. Too small =
=E2=86=92 constant disk reads (<a href=3D"#sizing--monitoring">sizing</a>)<=
/td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_buffer_pool_instances</code></td>
<td>8 (1 if pool &lt; 1 GB)</td>
<td>Splits the pool into independent parts to reduce mutex contention</td>
<td>Rarely; keep about 1 instance per GB, max 64</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_buffer_pool_dump_at_shutdown</code> / <code>_load_at_start=
up</code></td>
<td>ON / ON</td>
<td>Saves the list of cached pages at shutdown and reloads them at startup<=
/td>
<td>Keep ON: avoids a slow &quot;cold cache&quot; after restarts</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_old_blocks_pct</code> / <code>innodb_old_blocks_time</code=
></td>
<td>37 / 1000 ms</td>
<td>The LRU &quot;old&quot; sublist where new pages land first, and how lon=
g before they can be promoted, so one big scan can't flush the hot pages (<=
a href=3D"#eviction--which-page-gets-thrown-out">eviction</a>)</td>
<td>Rarely; raise the time if big scans keep evicting hot data</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_change_buffering</code></td>
<td><code>all</code></td>
<td>Buffers secondary-index changes for pages not in memory (<a href=3D"#th=
e-change-buffer--and-when-it-cant-save-you">change buffer</a>)</td>
<td><code>none</code> on fast SSDs, or when the pool holds the whole data s=
et</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_adaptive_hash_index</code></td>
<td>ON</td>
<td>Builds an in-memory hash index on hot B+ tree pages for faster lookups<=
/td>
<td>Turn OFF if <code>SHOW ENGINE INNODB STATUS</code> shows contention on =
it under heavy writes</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_log_buffer_size</code></td>
<td>16 MB</td>
<td>RAM buffer for redo records before they're written to the redo log</td>
<td>Raise (64=E2=80=93256 MB) for big transactions or very high write rates=
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_dedicated_server</code> =F0=9F=94=92</td>
<td>OFF</td>
<td>Auto-sizes the buffer pool, redo log and flush method from the server's=
 RAM</td>
<td>ON when MySQL is the only thing on the machine</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"durability--logging" data-toc=3D"Durability &amp; Logging">Durabi=
lity &amp; Logging</h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Flag</th>
<th>Default</th>
<th>What it controls</th>
<th>When to change</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_flush_log_at_trx_commit</code></td>
<td><strong>1</strong></td>
<td>When the redo log is written and <code>fsync</code>ed. <strong>1</stron=
g> =3D every commit (fully durable) =C2=B7 <strong>2</strong> =3D write eve=
ry commit, fsync every second =C2=B7 <strong>0</strong> =3D both once a sec=
ond (<a href=3D"#the-tuning-knobs-and-what-you-trade-away">details</a>)</td=
>
<td>Keep <strong>1</strong> for real data. 2 or 0 only where losing ~1 s of=
 commits is acceptable</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>sync_binlog</code> (server flag)</td>
<td><strong>1</strong></td>
<td>How often the <strong>binary log</strong> is fsynced. 1 =3D every commi=
t. Pair with the flag above (the &quot;double-1&quot; setting)</td>
<td>Keep <strong>1</strong> on any server used for replication or point-in-=
time recovery</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_redo_log_capacity</code></td>
<td>100 MB</td>
<td>Total redo log size (8.0.30+; replaces <code>innodb_log_file_size</code=
> =C3=97 <code>innodb_log_files_in_group</code>)</td>
<td>Too small =E2=86=92 frequent forced <a href=3D"#mechanism-3-checkpointi=
ng">checkpoints</a> and write stalls. Size it to hold about 1 hour of peak =
writes (often 2=E2=80=938 GB+)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_doublewrite</code> =F0=9F=94=92</td>
<td>ON</td>
<td>Writes pages to the <a href=3D"#mechanism-4-double-write-buffer--no-tor=
n-pages">doublewrite buffer</a> first, protecting against torn pages</td>
<td>Keep ON, unless the storage guarantees atomic 16 KB writes</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_flush_method</code> =F0=9F=94=92</td>
<td><code>fsync</code> (Linux)</td>
<td>How data files are written. <code>O_DIRECT</code> bypasses the OS page =
cache, so data isn't cached twice</td>
<td>Usually <code>O_DIRECT</code> on Linux with a large buffer pool</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_page_size</code> =F0=9F=94=92</td>
<td>16 KB</td>
<td>Size of every page</td>
<td>Only at instance creation; can't change later. Almost always leave it</=
td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"flushing--io-checkpointing" data-toc=3D"Flushing &amp; I/O (Check=
pointing)">Flushing &amp; I/O (Checkpointing)</h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Flag</th>
<th>Default</th>
<th>What it controls</th>
<th>When to change</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_io_capacity</code></td>
<td>200</td>
<td>IOPS InnoDB assumes for <strong>background</strong> work: flushing dirt=
y pages, merging the change buffer</td>
<td>SSD/NVMe: 1,000=E2=80=9310,000. Too low =E2=86=92 dirty pages pile up a=
nd checkpoints stall</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_io_capacity_max</code></td>
<td>2000</td>
<td>Upper IOPS limit when InnoDB has to flush harder</td>
<td>About 2=C3=97 <code>innodb_io_capacity</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_max_dirty_pages_pct</code></td>
<td>90</td>
<td>Max % of the buffer pool allowed to be <a href=3D"#key-terms--page-fram=
e-dirty-clean-pinned">dirty</a> before flushing gets aggressive</td>
<td>Rarely</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_max_dirty_pages_pct_lwm</code></td>
<td>10</td>
<td>Dirty % at which pre-flushing starts gently</td>
<td>Rarely</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_adaptive_flushing</code></td>
<td>ON</td>
<td>Adjusts flush speed based on how fast redo is being generated</td>
<td>Keep ON</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_page_cleaners</code></td>
<td>4</td>
<td>Number of background threads flushing dirty pages</td>
<td>Raise with many buffer pool instances and fast disks</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_flush_neighbors</code></td>
<td>0</td>
<td>Also flushes neighbouring dirty pages, which helps on HDDs</td>
<td>0 for SSD; 1 only for spinning disks</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_read_io_threads</code> / <code>innodb_write_io_threads</co=
de> =F0=9F=94=92</td>
<td>4 / 4</td>
<td>Background threads for async reads and writes</td>
<td>Raise on fast storage with many cores</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"locking--transactions" data-toc=3D"Locking &amp; Transactions">Lo=
cking &amp; Transactions</h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Flag</th>
<th>Default</th>
<th>What it controls</th>
<th>When to change</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>transaction_isolation</code> (server flag)</td>
<td><code>REPEATABLE-READ</code></td>
<td>Default <a href=3D"#sql-isolation-levels">isolation level</a> for new t=
ransactions</td>
<td>Many apps use <code>READ-COMMITTED</code> (fewer gap locks, fewer deadl=
ocks)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_lock_wait_timeout</code></td>
<td>50 s</td>
<td>How long a statement waits for a row lock before failing with &quot;Loc=
k wait timeout exceeded&quot;</td>
<td>Lower (e.g. 5=E2=80=9310 s) for web apps, so requests fail fast instead=
 of piling up</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_rollback_on_timeout</code> =F0=9F=94=92</td>
<td>OFF</td>
<td>On a lock-wait timeout, roll back only the <strong>last statement</stro=
ng> (OFF) or the <strong>whole transaction</strong> (ON)</td>
<td>=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F With OFF, the transaction stays open half-done. Your=
 code must <code>ROLLBACK</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_deadlock_detect</code></td>
<td>ON</td>
<td>Actively checks for <a href=3D"#deadlock-detection--the-wait-for-graph-=
wfg">deadlocks</a> and rolls back a victim immediately</td>
<td>Some very high-concurrency systems turn it OFF and rely on the lock-wai=
t timeout</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_print_all_deadlocks</code></td>
<td>OFF</td>
<td>Writes <strong>every</strong> deadlock to the error log (normally only =
the last one is kept, in <code>SHOW ENGINE INNODB STATUS</code>)</td>
<td>Turn ON to investigate recurring deadlocks</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_autoinc_lock_mode</code> =F0=9F=94=92</td>
<td>2</td>
<td>How <code>AUTO_INCREMENT</code> values are handed out. 2 (&quot;interle=
aved&quot;) is fastest, but IDs from concurrent bulk inserts may interleave=
 or have gaps</td>
<td>Keep 2 (needs row-based binlog, which is the default)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"undo--purge" data-toc=3D"Undo &amp; Purge">Undo &amp; Purge</h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Flag</th>
<th>Default</th>
<th>What it controls</th>
<th>When to change</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_purge_threads</code> =F0=9F=94=92</td>
<td>4</td>
<td>Background threads that remove old row versions and delete-marked rows<=
/td>
<td>Raise if <code>History list length</code> keeps growing (<a href=3D"#%E=
F%B8%8F-purge-lag--when-delete-backfires">purge lag</a>)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_max_purge_lag</code></td>
<td>0 (off)</td>
<td>Delays DML when purge falls too far behind, to let it catch up</td>
<td>Set only if history length grows out of control</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_undo_log_truncate</code></td>
<td>ON</td>
<td>Shrinks undo tablespaces once they grow too large</td>
<td>Keep ON</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_max_undo_log_size</code></td>
<td>1 GB</td>
<td>Size at which an undo tablespace gets truncated</td>
<td>Rarely</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<hr>
<h3 id=3D"tables-statistics--ddl" data-toc=3D"Tables, Statistics &amp; DDL"=
>Tables, Statistics &amp; DDL</h3>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Flag</th>
<th>Default</th>
<th>What it controls</th>
<th>When to change</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_file_per_table</code></td>
<td>ON</td>
<td>Each table in its own <code>.ibd</code> file (instead of one shared sys=
tem tablespace)</td>
<td>Keep ON: <code>DROP</code> / <code>TRUNCATE</code> actually free disk s=
pace</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_default_row_format</code></td>
<td><code>DYNAMIC</code></td>
<td>How rows (and long <code>TEXT</code>/<code>BLOB</code> values) are stor=
ed on pages</td>
<td>Keep <code>DYNAMIC</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_strict_mode</code></td>
<td>ON</td>
<td>Turns some <code>CREATE</code>/<code>ALTER</code> warnings into errors =
(e.g. impossible row sizes)</td>
<td>Keep ON</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_stats_persistent</code></td>
<td>ON</td>
<td>Index statistics (used by the optimizer) are stored on disk and survive=
 restarts</td>
<td>Keep ON</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_stats_persistent_sample_pages</code></td>
<td>20</td>
<td>Pages sampled per index when computing statistics (<a href=3D"#cardinal=
ity--selectivity--how-duplicate-values-affect-an-index">why it matters</a>)=
</td>
<td>Raise for big or skewed tables when <code>EXPLAIN</code> row estimates =
are badly off</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_stats_auto_recalc</code></td>
<td>ON</td>
<td>Recalculates statistics automatically after about 10% of a table's rows=
 change</td>
<td>Keep ON; run <code>ANALYZE TABLE</code> after big loads</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>innodb_online_alter_log_max_size</code></td>
<td>128 MB</td>
<td>Buffer for concurrent writes during an online <code>ALTER TABLE</code> =
(<a href=3D"#-what-happens-internally-when-we-run-an-alter-query-does-it-lo=
ck-the-table">online DDL</a>); if it fills, the <code>ALTER</code> fails</t=
d>
<td>Raise for long <code>ALTER</code>s on busy tables</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<hr>
